1
00:00:01,508 --> 00:00:04,007
(The Last Challenge)

2
00:00:04,008 --> 00:00:06,048
- Nice to see you all. - It's nice to see you.

3
00:00:06,818 --> 00:00:08,048
Gosh, Sung Hwan.

4
00:00:08,918 --> 00:00:10,798
Are you the same old Sung Hwan we used to know?

5
00:00:11,188 --> 00:00:13,288
- You look great. - How much weight did you lose?

6
00:00:13,718 --> 00:00:16,627
I lost about 12kg if you want a specific number.

7
00:00:16,628 --> 00:00:18,897
But I didn't lose weight by going on a diet.

8
00:00:18,898 --> 00:00:20,234
- Okay. - How did you lose weight then?

9
00:00:20,258 --> 00:00:23,168
Since I was in my 20s, I had this dream...

10
00:00:23,828 --> 00:00:26,837
- about my bucket list. - Okay.

11
00:00:26,838 --> 00:00:29,037
I failed twice in my 20s to check it off my bucket list.

12
00:00:29,038 --> 00:00:30,667
- In your 20s? - Yes, in my 20s.

13
00:00:30,668 --> 00:00:33,808
I wanted to give it another try before I hit 50.

14
00:00:34,178 --> 00:00:36,148
- But if I fail again this time, - That's it?

15
00:00:36,378 --> 00:00:37,648
I'd never try it again.

16
00:00:37,808 --> 00:00:39,517
So I gave it my all...

17
00:00:39,518 --> 00:00:43,248
to my last challenge in my 40s from the bottom of my heart.

18
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:47,017
You can watch to find out whether I failed or succeeded.

19
00:00:47,018 --> 00:00:48,787
- Your energy level says it all. - Right.

20
00:00:48,788 --> 00:00:49,987
- Right? - He sounds like he succeeded.

21
00:00:49,988 --> 00:00:52,027
- It would be funny if he failed. - To see if I failed or succeeded...

22
00:00:52,028 --> 00:00:54,027
- But you never know. - Okay.

23
00:00:54,028 --> 00:00:55,827
He was also cheerful when he failed the license test.

24
00:00:55,828 --> 00:00:57,068
You're right.

25
00:00:57,768 --> 00:00:59,538
(Let's find out.)

26
00:01:00,138 --> 00:01:01,197
(Ku Walks Across the Country)

27
00:01:01,198 --> 00:01:03,118
"Ku Walks Across the Country." Oh, this is nice.

28
00:01:04,868 --> 00:01:10,808
(Sung Hwan is sleeping like a log.)

29
00:01:16,548 --> 00:01:17,947
(Current time, 6:05am)

30
00:01:17,948 --> 00:01:19,118
It's 6:05am.

31
00:01:20,058 --> 00:01:23,628
(Tossing and turning)

32
00:01:24,228 --> 00:01:27,798
(What time is it?)

33
00:01:29,098 --> 00:01:31,268
(Turning off the alarm)

34
00:01:32,468 --> 00:01:36,468
(He wakes up even before dawn breaks.)

35
00:01:38,368 --> 00:01:39,538
Gosh, this is killing me.

36
00:01:42,238 --> 00:01:44,108
Oh, my legs. Goodness.

37
00:01:45,478 --> 00:01:46,617
Gosh, my legs.

38
00:01:46,618 --> 00:01:49,788
(He gets up while groaning in pain.)

39
00:01:51,548 --> 00:01:52,758
My body aches.

40
00:01:53,158 --> 00:01:54,457
- You've gotten so slim. - My goodness.

41
00:01:54,458 --> 00:01:55,758
I've never seen you this thin.

42
00:01:56,458 --> 00:01:57,527
My goodness.

43
00:01:57,528 --> 00:01:58,627
(His legs are covered with relief patches.)

44
00:01:58,628 --> 00:01:59,868
- Relief patches... - So far...

45
00:02:01,928 --> 00:02:03,167
Look at my feet. They got so tanned.

46
00:02:03,168 --> 00:02:04,808
I thought you were already wearing socks.

47
00:02:09,468 --> 00:02:15,338
(Familiar clothes are hanging in an unfamiliar room.)

48
00:02:16,278 --> 00:02:19,048
(Lying back down)

49
00:02:19,918 --> 00:02:24,087
(Sung Hwan is struggling to move around.)

50
00:02:24,088 --> 00:02:25,188
Gosh, my back.

51
00:02:26,718 --> 00:02:28,857
I'm at the community center of Anmak 1-gu...

52
00:02:28,858 --> 00:02:31,587
in Gimhae, South Gyeongsang Province.

53
00:02:31,588 --> 00:02:33,468
- The community center? - The community center?

54
00:02:33,628 --> 00:02:36,628
Right now, I'm walking across the country...

55
00:02:36,928 --> 00:02:38,727
- from Seoul to Busan. - Walk across the country?

56
00:02:38,728 --> 00:02:40,868
- Walk across the country? - I love this.

57
00:02:41,168 --> 00:02:44,968
A lot of people have walking across the country...

58
00:02:45,108 --> 00:02:47,578
on their bucket list.

59
00:02:47,938 --> 00:02:51,778
Walking across the country...

60
00:02:52,078 --> 00:02:54,147
is the most romantic challenge I can think of.

61
00:02:54,148 --> 00:02:55,178
That's true.

62
00:02:55,718 --> 00:02:57,547
I tried this 2 times when I was in my 20s.

63
00:02:57,548 --> 00:02:58,817
(I tried this 2 times when I was in my 20s.)

64
00:02:58,818 --> 00:03:00,588
Then I failed both times.

65
00:03:01,218 --> 00:03:03,728
This is my last challenge.

66
00:03:05,628 --> 00:03:06,827
(It was 2004.)

67
00:03:06,828 --> 00:03:08,197
- What? - What's this?

68
00:03:08,198 --> 00:03:09,528
- What? - My gosh.

69
00:03:09,928 --> 00:03:11,497
Were you really in your 20s?

70
00:03:11,498 --> 00:03:14,067
That was 2004.

71
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:15,238
- At first... - Who's this?

72
00:03:15,438 --> 00:03:16,637
- What? - What?

73
00:03:16,638 --> 00:03:18,808
(He was full of youth and motivation.)

74
00:03:19,138 --> 00:03:22,648
I think I'll probably arrive in Sokcho sometime next week.

75
00:03:24,048 --> 00:03:26,518
It's been two weeks. But I'm not feeling well.

76
00:03:27,118 --> 00:03:29,017
It's no joke. I'm covered in blisters.

77
00:03:29,018 --> 00:03:30,618
(His condition suddenly got worse.)

78
00:03:30,918 --> 00:03:34,918
During my first try, I got plantar fasciitis.

79
00:03:35,158 --> 00:03:36,257
So I failed.

80
00:03:36,258 --> 00:03:37,988
I was able to walk to Sokcho, though.

81
00:03:38,428 --> 00:03:40,058
Ever since then,

82
00:03:40,328 --> 00:03:41,997
I always had this thought in the back of my mind...

83
00:03:41,998 --> 00:03:43,628
that I would try it again someday.

84
00:03:44,128 --> 00:03:45,328
Then...

85
00:03:46,268 --> 00:03:49,808
my dog had been with me for 11 years.

86
00:03:50,338 --> 00:03:51,538
Kkotbun...

87
00:03:52,578 --> 00:03:56,348
Losing her out of the blue like that...

88
00:03:58,408 --> 00:04:01,978
took a huge emotional toll on me, I guess.

89
00:04:02,548 --> 00:04:04,829
Of course, it's understandable. She was like my daughter.

90
00:04:05,388 --> 00:04:06,488
I wanted to...

91
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:08,487
break away from this sense of loss.

92
00:04:08,488 --> 00:04:11,888
And walking was the method I chose to do that.

93
00:04:12,258 --> 00:04:14,057
I bet that motivated you even more.

94
00:04:14,058 --> 00:04:17,198
It was really helpful. I mean it.

95
00:04:17,868 --> 00:04:20,568
I set out on my third challenge of walking...

96
00:04:21,298 --> 00:04:23,308
from my home in Cheonho-dong...

97
00:04:24,038 --> 00:04:25,568
to Gwangalli Beach in Busan.

98
00:04:25,908 --> 00:04:27,508
- The distance was 446km. - Gosh, 446km.

99
00:04:27,908 --> 00:04:29,508
That's running 11 full course marathons.

100
00:04:30,148 --> 00:04:31,707
I'll walk across the country.

101
00:04:31,708 --> 00:04:35,078
I'm starting my cross-country journey today.

102
00:04:35,418 --> 00:04:36,847
- How old were you in the video? - No.

103
00:04:36,848 --> 00:04:39,787
(How old were you in the video?)

104
00:04:39,788 --> 00:04:41,718
I can't tell your age in the videos.

105
00:04:41,818 --> 00:04:43,827
That was the first day of my journey.

106
00:04:43,828 --> 00:04:44,888
It was your first day?

107
00:04:45,028 --> 00:04:46,427
- He does look younger. - His first day.

108
00:04:46,428 --> 00:04:48,327
(He does look younger.)

109
00:04:48,328 --> 00:04:50,267
I'm not sure if I will fail or succeed.

110
00:04:50,268 --> 00:04:53,298
But here I go.

111
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,198
My gosh, I'm nervous.

112
00:04:56,138 --> 00:04:57,208
Let's go!

113
00:04:57,468 --> 00:04:59,038
As for my condition on Day One,

114
00:04:59,838 --> 00:05:02,508
my feet and knees are good so far.

115
00:05:03,108 --> 00:05:04,677
Let's go!

116
00:05:04,678 --> 00:05:06,678
- He looks good on his first day. - Let's go.

117
00:05:07,778 --> 00:05:08,878
What a cool view.

118
00:05:09,448 --> 00:05:11,117
(Even in rain...)

119
00:05:11,118 --> 00:05:12,487
My gosh, when it rained...

120
00:05:12,488 --> 00:05:13,687
- Right. - It was hailing too?

121
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:14,788
- Hail... - Gosh.

122
00:05:15,858 --> 00:05:18,828
(To make things worse, even when his feet hurt...)

123
00:05:19,628 --> 00:05:22,727
I'm going to turn 50 soon.

124
00:05:22,728 --> 00:05:25,268
But I wanted to give it a try no matter what.

125
00:05:26,438 --> 00:05:28,698
If you can't avoid it, have fun with it.

126
00:05:30,668 --> 00:05:32,308
(While enjoying all kinds of hardships, )

127
00:05:33,338 --> 00:05:36,477
(he walked a total of...)

128
00:05:36,478 --> 00:05:37,608
I have...

129
00:05:37,778 --> 00:05:39,718
- Yangsan. - only 20km left to Busan.

130
00:05:40,118 --> 00:05:41,178
He walked 421km?

131
00:05:41,878 --> 00:05:43,418
I'm really close to the end.

132
00:05:44,618 --> 00:05:46,158
I might tear up. Seriously.

133
00:05:46,988 --> 00:05:51,528
For the past 16 days, I walked 421km.

134
00:05:52,488 --> 00:05:53,828
Today is my last day.

135
00:05:54,798 --> 00:05:56,998
To reach Gwangalli in Busan from Gimhae,

136
00:05:57,368 --> 00:05:59,337
I just need to walk 25km more.

137
00:05:59,338 --> 00:06:01,338
- It's my big finale. - Gosh, 25km.

138
00:06:01,838 --> 00:06:04,238
Then how many days did it take for you to finish?

139
00:06:04,738 --> 00:06:07,877
I initially planned to finish the walk in 14 days.

140
00:06:07,878 --> 00:06:10,208
I had to keep walking, so I wasn't feeling well.

141
00:06:10,678 --> 00:06:15,117
I kept increasing the total distance because I got more ambitious.

142
00:06:15,118 --> 00:06:16,888
So I ended up adding three more days.

143
00:06:17,288 --> 00:06:20,057
It became an 18-day journey according to my plan.

144
00:06:20,058 --> 00:06:21,787
- Eighteen days. - You can adjust the days, I guess.

145
00:06:21,788 --> 00:06:24,387
Then you'll release about 18 episodes?

146
00:06:24,388 --> 00:06:25,587
Not that long.

147
00:06:25,588 --> 00:06:27,434
- This is... - The runner is getting competitive.

148
00:06:27,458 --> 00:06:28,997
Right. He's getting competitive.

149
00:06:28,998 --> 00:06:30,597
- Out of 18 days... - No.

150
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:31,797
- Those 18 days... - He's the icon...

151
00:06:31,798 --> 00:06:33,238
- of challenges. - That's his thing.

152
00:06:33,398 --> 00:06:35,737
My gosh. Don't say that.

153
00:06:35,738 --> 00:06:37,838
- You're stealing his thing. - It's for everyone.

154
00:06:38,068 --> 00:06:39,678
Hey, I won't do another challenge.

155
00:06:40,208 --> 00:06:41,508
Don't forget my Fun Run.

156
00:06:41,608 --> 00:06:42,907
- Just don't throw up. - Right.

157
00:06:42,908 --> 00:06:44,547
- Don't throw up. - You keep bringing that up.

158
00:06:44,548 --> 00:06:45,777
(Okay. I'll let you have it.)

159
00:06:45,778 --> 00:06:47,217
Didn't you walk to Busan, MINHO?

160
00:06:47,218 --> 00:06:50,047
- I went from Busan to Seoul. - Right?

161
00:06:50,048 --> 00:06:51,117
- Did you walk? - Really?

162
00:06:51,118 --> 00:06:52,717
- I rode my bicycle. - I see.

163
00:06:52,718 --> 00:06:54,457
- Gosh, no. I rode my bicycle. - Okay.

164
00:06:54,458 --> 00:06:56,157
- You know what? - What a relief.

165
00:06:56,158 --> 00:06:58,057
Don't share that story today. Let him take all the spotlight.

166
00:06:58,058 --> 00:06:59,427
- Right. He should. - Stop it.

167
00:06:59,428 --> 00:07:01,328
- Okay. - I almost died.

168
00:07:02,298 --> 00:07:03,468
My gosh, I'm tired.

169
00:07:04,028 --> 00:07:06,697
A friend of mine introduced me to this place.

170
00:07:06,698 --> 00:07:08,137
It's a community center...

171
00:07:08,138 --> 00:07:09,538
- in Anmak. - The lodging?

172
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:11,968
I'm not feeling well.

173
00:07:14,038 --> 00:07:20,148
(The long, tiring journey has weakened his body and mind.)

174
00:07:21,018 --> 00:07:24,418
(He just has to keep pushing for one more day.)

175
00:07:25,348 --> 00:07:26,417
He definitely...

176
00:07:26,418 --> 00:07:28,617
- looks the worst I've ever seen. - Right. Because...

177
00:07:28,618 --> 00:07:30,688
- Right. - It's harder toward the end.

178
00:07:31,628 --> 00:07:33,298
Hold on. Let me check the weather.

179
00:07:35,098 --> 00:07:36,228
My goodness.

180
00:07:37,028 --> 00:07:38,098
Oh, my legs.

181
00:07:38,798 --> 00:07:39,997
Gosh, today...

182
00:07:39,998 --> 00:07:41,438
(Let's see.)

183
00:07:41,898 --> 00:07:44,508
It said it would rain in the afternoon, so I got up early.

184
00:07:45,308 --> 00:07:46,938
Gosh, it will rain all day.

185
00:07:48,338 --> 00:07:51,347
Why did it have to rain on my last day? This is annoying.

186
00:07:51,348 --> 00:07:52,748
(Why on my last day of all days?)

187
00:07:53,278 --> 00:07:54,377
Hongga.

188
00:07:54,378 --> 00:07:55,378
Hongga?

189
00:07:55,379 --> 00:07:56,547
Wake up.

190
00:07:56,548 --> 00:07:57,588
He must be his colleague.

191
00:07:59,218 --> 00:08:00,758
It's raining outside.

192
00:08:00,918 --> 00:08:02,488
(Groaning)

193
00:08:06,298 --> 00:08:08,228
It's...

194
00:08:09,158 --> 00:08:10,328
It's...

195
00:08:10,628 --> 00:08:11,968
- He startled me. - What?

196
00:08:12,498 --> 00:08:13,837
(What was that just now?)

197
00:08:13,838 --> 00:08:15,098
I thought it was his dad.

198
00:08:15,238 --> 00:08:17,078
- This isn't "The Roundup," right? - It's not.

199
00:08:17,208 --> 00:08:18,307
He's not from the movies.

200
00:08:18,308 --> 00:08:19,748
- He's my actual friend. - He's not?

201
00:08:20,878 --> 00:08:24,207
It's not raining that hard for now. But it is still raining.

202
00:08:24,208 --> 00:08:25,568
(His partner has an intense look.)

203
00:08:28,518 --> 00:08:31,548
His name is Hong Yu Chang.

204
00:08:32,018 --> 00:08:33,018
He's a rapper.

205
00:08:33,019 --> 00:08:34,457
- And his stage name is Hongga. - He's a rapper?

206
00:08:34,458 --> 00:08:36,188
- He's a rapper. - He's my senior rapper.

207
00:08:36,588 --> 00:08:39,528
We've been friends for seven years.

208
00:08:39,858 --> 00:08:42,228
He went on most trips with me and Kkotbun...

209
00:08:42,768 --> 00:08:44,728
out of all my friends.

210
00:08:45,468 --> 00:08:47,238
I bet he raps aggressively.

211
00:08:47,868 --> 00:08:49,538
- No. He's really mellow. - Really?

212
00:08:51,108 --> 00:08:53,507
Kkotbun probably spent the most time...

213
00:08:53,508 --> 00:08:55,338
with him after Ju Seung.

214
00:08:55,678 --> 00:08:57,148
He's like family.

215
00:08:57,478 --> 00:08:59,007
- Was he... - It's raining outside.

216
00:08:59,008 --> 00:09:00,577
- with you for the whole walk? - Yes, he was.

217
00:09:00,578 --> 00:09:02,378
- Really? - You must be so grateful.

218
00:09:02,518 --> 00:09:04,588
I told him I was leaving tomorrow to do this.

219
00:09:04,718 --> 00:09:05,817
He told me it was on his bucket list...

220
00:09:05,818 --> 00:09:07,318
and wanted to try it for a long time.

221
00:09:07,718 --> 00:09:09,858
He asked me if he could join me.

222
00:09:10,428 --> 00:09:12,927
I told him it was a big decision and he needed to be ready.

223
00:09:12,928 --> 00:09:15,228
- Right. - Then we decided to do it together.

224
00:09:15,358 --> 00:09:17,797
- He's so innocent. - He is.

225
00:09:17,798 --> 00:09:19,598
I guess you're close to him too.

226
00:09:19,868 --> 00:09:21,638
I thought Ju Seung would do it with him.

227
00:09:21,868 --> 00:09:24,268
Ju Seung would be too fast because he'd just use shukuchi.

228
00:09:25,108 --> 00:09:26,388
He could get there in four days.

229
00:09:27,138 --> 00:09:28,277
Our pace would be different.

230
00:09:28,278 --> 00:09:29,838
(You needed 17 days? I can do it in 4.)

231
00:09:30,648 --> 00:09:33,377
(He checks on the laundry as soon as he gets up.)

232
00:09:33,378 --> 00:09:34,448
Did you get some sleep?

233
00:09:34,848 --> 00:09:35,918
My shoulders hurt.

234
00:09:37,588 --> 00:09:40,458
(His walking partner folds the laundry first.)

235
00:09:42,058 --> 00:09:44,358
(Grunting)

236
00:09:44,728 --> 00:09:46,698
I felt like a soldier who fought in 100 battles.

237
00:09:47,028 --> 00:09:49,698
It wasn't just localized pain. My whole body ached.

238
00:09:50,598 --> 00:09:53,097
(Groaning)

239
00:09:53,098 --> 00:09:56,138
Hey, today is our last day, by the way.

240
00:09:57,568 --> 00:09:59,878
I guess we're nearing the end, after all.

241
00:10:00,738 --> 00:10:02,008
But it's killing me.

242
00:10:04,808 --> 00:10:05,977
- Gosh. - My goodness.

243
00:10:05,978 --> 00:10:07,517
- That's cute. - His forehead got tanned.

244
00:10:07,518 --> 00:10:08,917
His forehead...

245
00:10:08,918 --> 00:10:10,917
- That's special effects makeup. - Is that makeup?

246
00:10:10,918 --> 00:10:12,588
He has garaetteok on his forehead.

247
00:10:14,818 --> 00:10:16,588
Doesn't it look like a halo?

248
00:10:17,028 --> 00:10:18,628
- Ding. - The halo around angels.

249
00:10:19,458 --> 00:10:20,928
He looks like a celestial rapper.

250
00:10:22,558 --> 00:10:25,998
- Right. We walked for 16 days. - Yes.

251
00:10:26,198 --> 00:10:27,797
- He wore a headband. - Yes.

252
00:10:27,798 --> 00:10:29,068
He sweats a lot.

253
00:10:29,338 --> 00:10:32,208
Wearing a hat for nine hours was uncomfortable for him.

254
00:10:32,508 --> 00:10:34,837
- He applied a lot of sunscreen. - He did, right?

255
00:10:34,838 --> 00:10:35,977
But he still got tanned like that.

256
00:10:35,978 --> 00:10:36,978
(Their 16-day walk beat sunscreen.)

257
00:10:36,979 --> 00:10:38,578
(He still finds it funny.)

258
00:10:38,978 --> 00:10:41,278
We have to get ready fast. It's raining.

259
00:10:44,048 --> 00:10:45,117
That must hurt.

260
00:10:45,118 --> 00:10:46,188
My gosh.

261
00:10:46,788 --> 00:10:48,148
Relief patches aren't working now.

262
00:10:49,288 --> 00:10:50,328
Relief patches...

263
00:10:50,628 --> 00:10:53,028
But you look super young.

264
00:10:53,498 --> 00:10:54,527
He looks younger...

265
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:56,248
- than when he was in his 20s. - Sung Hwan.

266
00:10:58,398 --> 00:11:00,798
(Limping)

267
00:11:01,638 --> 00:11:03,938
(He tries to get ready quickly despite his tired body.)

268
00:11:04,738 --> 00:11:06,067
(Getting up)

269
00:11:06,068 --> 00:11:07,808
Let's tidy up this place.

270
00:11:09,278 --> 00:11:13,647
(Hongga finishes tidying up his things before Sung Hwan.)

271
00:11:13,648 --> 00:11:16,888
(Getting on the foam roller)

272
00:11:17,048 --> 00:11:18,388
Look how tanned his thighs are.

273
00:11:18,488 --> 00:11:19,717
- Gosh, that's crazy. - Oh, my.

274
00:11:19,718 --> 00:11:20,787
(A clear tan line)

275
00:11:20,788 --> 00:11:21,988
UV rays are no joke.

276
00:11:22,588 --> 00:11:24,728
(Soon after, Sung Hwan also...)

277
00:11:26,898 --> 00:11:28,197
This is the best.

278
00:11:28,198 --> 00:11:29,318
(starts massaging his feet.)

279
00:11:29,628 --> 00:11:31,067
(It hurts, but it feels good.)

280
00:11:31,068 --> 00:11:33,338
- That must hurt. - It hurts, but it feels so good.

281
00:11:33,868 --> 00:11:36,438
(Doing his best)

282
00:11:37,308 --> 00:11:40,138
(After thoroughly massaging their muscles...)

283
00:11:41,078 --> 00:11:42,238
How are your feet?

284
00:11:43,378 --> 00:11:44,508
The blisters...

285
00:11:45,748 --> 00:11:49,148
Once the old ones are gone, I get new ones. That repeats.

286
00:11:52,318 --> 00:11:53,487
It's a blister.

287
00:11:53,488 --> 00:11:55,857
(His toes are covered in blisters.)

288
00:11:55,858 --> 00:11:56,958
Underneath...

289
00:11:57,728 --> 00:11:59,358
(Oh, no.)

290
00:11:59,758 --> 00:12:00,828
Doesn't it hurt?

291
00:12:01,358 --> 00:12:03,198
- My feet didn't get blisters. - Underneath?

292
00:12:03,498 --> 00:12:04,827
But his feet were covered in blisters.

293
00:12:04,828 --> 00:12:06,598
My gosh. Oh, no.

294
00:12:07,168 --> 00:12:10,208
I'm in charge of breakfast. So I'll cook.

295
00:12:10,538 --> 00:12:12,667
Do you want your usual amount?

296
00:12:12,668 --> 00:12:14,108
Okay. Sounds good.

297
00:12:15,178 --> 00:12:16,247
Okay.

298
00:12:16,248 --> 00:12:18,048
(Grabbing)

299
00:12:19,978 --> 00:12:21,078
The SKJ...

300
00:12:21,148 --> 00:12:22,318
Ramyeon.

301
00:12:22,918 --> 00:12:26,217
(He fills the pot with water.)

302
00:12:26,218 --> 00:12:27,358
It's on.

303
00:12:29,488 --> 00:12:31,788
We had to eat carbs in the morning no matter what.

304
00:12:32,858 --> 00:12:34,528
(Adding the noodles from jjajang ramyeon)

305
00:12:35,598 --> 00:12:39,298
(Then he also adds noodles from kalguksu ramyeon...)

306
00:12:40,068 --> 00:12:41,237
(and the squid-flavored ramyeon too.)

307
00:12:41,238 --> 00:12:42,744
- What kind of combo is this? - That's it.

308
00:12:42,768 --> 00:12:44,108
I call it SKJ.

309
00:12:45,368 --> 00:12:46,637
It has squid-flavored ramyeon,

310
00:12:46,638 --> 00:12:49,108
- Kalguksu. - the anchovy kalguksu ramyeon,

311
00:12:49,578 --> 00:12:50,707
and jjajang ramyeon.

312
00:12:50,708 --> 00:12:53,618
Together, I call it SKJ. It's really good.

313
00:12:56,048 --> 00:12:58,848
(Cooking fried eggs to eat with the ramyeon)

314
00:12:59,218 --> 00:13:01,088
(Meanwhile, Hongga...)

315
00:13:01,858 --> 00:13:04,588
(sets up a place to eat without being told to do so.)

316
00:13:05,958 --> 00:13:08,257
- That looks good. - I wonder how it tastes.

317
00:13:08,258 --> 00:13:11,198
The noodles look nice and thick. I bet it tastes good.

318
00:13:11,328 --> 00:13:13,538
That looks amazing. I'd love to try it.

319
00:13:14,368 --> 00:13:15,738
All done. Let's eat.

320
00:13:16,308 --> 00:13:19,068
It's called SKJ ramyeon.

321
00:13:19,978 --> 00:13:23,208
Try the good, old SKJ ramyeon. It's been a while. Eat a lot.

322
00:13:24,578 --> 00:13:26,277
(Loading up on noodles to save energy)

323
00:13:26,278 --> 00:13:28,348
- The noodles got soggy. - We must eat them fast.

324
00:13:30,888 --> 00:13:33,318
They didn't get too soggy. They're perfect.

325
00:13:34,388 --> 00:13:36,018
Gosh, that looks really good.

326
00:13:36,258 --> 00:13:37,898
- With the noodles... - It looks so good.

327
00:13:39,858 --> 00:13:42,058
(I need some protein to get some strength for the day.)

328
00:13:43,028 --> 00:13:46,198
I love having noodles like this for breakfast. It's so good.

329
00:13:47,798 --> 00:13:49,467
- Like ramyeon at orientations. - You can taste the jjajang sauce...

330
00:13:49,468 --> 00:13:50,537
and the seafood.

331
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:52,837
- You get the anchovy flavor too. - Gosh, that sounds so good.

332
00:13:52,838 --> 00:13:54,808
- It must taste so good with kimchi. - Yes.

333
00:13:55,838 --> 00:13:58,177
My gosh. This is crazy, right?

334
00:13:58,178 --> 00:13:59,178
(Nodding)

335
00:14:00,178 --> 00:14:02,078
(Slurping)

336
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:06,638
We haven't had it in a while. It tastes so good.

337
00:14:07,518 --> 00:14:09,318
(We must eat up for energy.)

338
00:14:10,128 --> 00:14:11,188
That was so good.

339
00:14:12,988 --> 00:14:17,128
(Gobbling up the food to complete the journey)

340
00:14:20,598 --> 00:14:22,738
- I know how much you eat. - Don't eat too much.

341
00:14:22,868 --> 00:14:24,268
This is my last bite.

342
00:14:25,368 --> 00:14:26,808
I'll keep on eating if there's food.

343
00:14:27,078 --> 00:14:28,478
I'll get tired while walking later.

344
00:14:30,148 --> 00:14:32,378
(You're right.)

345
00:14:33,078 --> 00:14:35,578
- Wait. He has those baby eyes. - Yes.

346
00:14:35,818 --> 00:14:37,087
- They resemble each other. - He has kind eyes.

347
00:14:37,088 --> 00:14:38,424
- He has those pure baby eyes. - Yes.

348
00:14:38,448 --> 00:14:40,057
- He looks like a baby too. - He resembles an infant.

349
00:14:40,058 --> 00:14:41,157
- An infant? - Right.

350
00:14:41,158 --> 00:14:43,687
- Remove the beard. And he's a baby. - He's a baby.

351
00:14:43,688 --> 00:14:45,128
- Right. - He does look like a baby.

352
00:14:45,158 --> 00:14:46,328
I'll clean up.

353
00:14:47,098 --> 00:14:48,228
Take your time.

354
00:14:49,098 --> 00:14:50,167
I'm done.

355
00:14:50,168 --> 00:14:51,648
Can you remove the wooden chopsticks?

356
00:14:51,868 --> 00:14:53,868
- Take care of the trash for me. - Okay.

357
00:14:54,898 --> 00:14:58,108
(Sung Hwan washes the dishes.)

358
00:15:00,678 --> 00:15:02,738
(Hongga cleans up.)

359
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:07,218
(The fantastic duo finishes in no time with their teamwork.)

360
00:15:07,978 --> 00:15:09,618
(Checking his phone)

361
00:15:11,548 --> 00:15:12,687
I need to get ready.

362
00:15:12,688 --> 00:15:14,088
(Hongga is engrossed in something.)

363
00:15:15,758 --> 00:15:17,157
(Checking their route for the day)

364
00:15:17,158 --> 00:15:19,087
- It's the map. - We have different tasks...

365
00:15:19,088 --> 00:15:20,998
in the morning.

366
00:15:22,158 --> 00:15:24,498
I have no sense of direction and everyone knows it.

367
00:15:24,768 --> 00:15:26,838
But Hongga has the best sense of direction.

368
00:15:27,068 --> 00:15:29,907
That's why we divided up our responsibilities.

369
00:15:29,908 --> 00:15:33,038
Hongga's role is finding the path like the GPS.

370
00:15:33,438 --> 00:15:35,338
My role is coming up with the schedule...

371
00:15:35,538 --> 00:15:36,878
and cooking.

372
00:15:37,248 --> 00:15:38,948
That's how we split up our roles.

373
00:15:39,378 --> 00:15:42,218
- Then you definitely needed him. - Yes.

374
00:15:42,778 --> 00:15:44,347
(Sitting down)

375
00:15:44,348 --> 00:15:45,418
Oh, right.

376
00:15:46,418 --> 00:15:48,787
How much did we walk yesterday?

377
00:15:48,788 --> 00:15:50,287
- Wait. Let me check. - Okay.

378
00:15:50,288 --> 00:15:52,428
(The Walking GPS calculates it right away.)

379
00:15:52,558 --> 00:15:54,698
We walked 24km yesterday.

380
00:15:54,858 --> 00:15:56,598
- He... Yes. - He wrote everything down.

381
00:15:56,898 --> 00:15:58,297
You need to record everything.

382
00:15:58,298 --> 00:15:59,368
So,

383
00:16:00,398 --> 00:16:01,468
with that,

384
00:16:02,598 --> 00:16:03,738
we'll arrive here.

385
00:16:04,168 --> 00:16:06,237
Give it to me. Gosh, this is the big day.

386
00:16:06,238 --> 00:16:08,378
(Overwhelmed)

387
00:16:09,178 --> 00:16:11,347
Is this our 16th day? Or the 17th day?

388
00:16:11,348 --> 00:16:12,348
That's confusing.

389
00:16:12,349 --> 00:16:13,577
- He's so thorough. - It's our 17th day.

390
00:16:13,578 --> 00:16:15,877
Toward the end, your pace slowed down.

391
00:16:15,878 --> 00:16:17,417
- It slowed down a lot. - Right, it did.

392
00:16:17,418 --> 00:16:18,618
That's a really cool record.

393
00:16:18,718 --> 00:16:20,217
It's our last day. It's D-Day.

394
00:16:20,218 --> 00:16:21,934
(The day they will complete their long 17-day walking journey)

395
00:16:21,958 --> 00:16:24,688
- We just have to walk 25km today. - We have to walk 25km today.

396
00:16:25,188 --> 00:16:28,398
But we might have to walk 1km more.

397
00:16:28,458 --> 00:16:30,028
- When we finish... - So 25km...

398
00:16:30,498 --> 00:16:33,438
That gives us a total distance of 446km, right?

399
00:16:33,638 --> 00:16:37,568
- Later... - Our initial goal was 425km.

400
00:16:38,108 --> 00:16:39,938
- But we increased it by 20km. - Okay.

401
00:16:42,078 --> 00:16:44,047
Do you know what I noticed...

402
00:16:44,048 --> 00:16:45,978
when I rode my bicycle from Busan to Seoul?

403
00:16:46,248 --> 00:16:48,247
I had to climb over a mountain while passing through...

404
00:16:48,248 --> 00:16:50,408
North Gyeongsang Province. There was no way around it.

405
00:16:50,448 --> 00:16:51,448
There was no other path.

406
00:16:51,449 --> 00:16:52,888
When I was climbing, I thought,

407
00:16:53,358 --> 00:16:54,958
"My gosh. This isn't right."

408
00:16:55,158 --> 00:16:57,078
"I can't do this." I didn't think I could do it.

409
00:16:57,258 --> 00:17:00,728
- But there was a downward path too. - Right.

410
00:17:00,998 --> 00:17:02,698
- That boosted my energy then. - Right.

411
00:17:02,828 --> 00:17:05,398
There's no shortcut while walking across the country.

412
00:17:05,498 --> 00:17:08,067
Let's say you want to rest for one more hour.

413
00:17:08,068 --> 00:17:09,967
- Then you must walk more later. - Right.

414
00:17:09,968 --> 00:17:11,837
There's no homework. If it's an uphill path, you just walk.

415
00:17:11,838 --> 00:17:12,838
If you put it off,

416
00:17:12,839 --> 00:17:14,177
- it's harder the next day. Right. - I must walk more the next day.

417
00:17:14,178 --> 00:17:15,338
It will be more tiring.

418
00:17:15,838 --> 00:17:17,008
You got a life lesson.

419
00:17:18,508 --> 00:17:19,947
(After checking the remaining distance...)

420
00:17:19,948 --> 00:17:21,018
- We're set. - Okay.

421
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:28,418
(Getting ready one last time with determination)

422
00:17:29,758 --> 00:17:31,128
(Grabbing)

423
00:17:32,458 --> 00:17:35,627
(Taping their knees to complete the journey)

424
00:17:35,628 --> 00:17:37,168
We have to tape our knees well.

425
00:17:37,568 --> 00:17:39,048
It's an anti-inflammatory painkiller.

426
00:17:39,828 --> 00:17:41,297
(Going into battle on painkillers)

427
00:17:41,298 --> 00:17:43,138
- I can sense your determination. - Yes.

428
00:17:44,338 --> 00:17:46,778
(Getting ready smoothly)

429
00:17:48,338 --> 00:17:49,908
(Taking it out)

430
00:17:51,078 --> 00:17:52,348
Help me put this on.

431
00:17:53,248 --> 00:17:54,578
- What's that? - What is it?

432
00:17:56,148 --> 00:17:57,248
She should...

433
00:17:58,288 --> 00:17:59,788
walk with me today.

434
00:18:01,788 --> 00:18:04,487
I had bought other things for Kkotbun. But she had always...

435
00:18:04,488 --> 00:18:06,288
worn this leash since she was two months old.

436
00:18:06,358 --> 00:18:08,627
- Kkotbun's leash. - It's Kkotbun's leash? Gosh.

437
00:18:08,628 --> 00:18:10,027
I wore the leash on my wrist.

438
00:18:10,028 --> 00:18:12,628
It helped me tremendously when it got really tough.

439
00:18:12,968 --> 00:18:15,737
I would say, "Gosh, I'm so tired." Then I would look at it.

440
00:18:15,738 --> 00:18:17,338
Strangely, it gave me a bit more energy.

441
00:18:17,408 --> 00:18:20,408
That's the fascinating thing about dogs.

442
00:18:21,038 --> 00:18:23,907
They give us a reason to keep living when they're alive.

443
00:18:23,908 --> 00:18:25,707
But even when they're gone, they still push us to live.

444
00:18:25,708 --> 00:18:27,477
- Right. - It was the same with me.

445
00:18:27,478 --> 00:18:29,118
- That's really fascinating. - I see.

446
00:18:30,548 --> 00:18:33,087
Even Kkotbun walked across the country.

447
00:18:33,088 --> 00:18:35,817
(Kkotbun has been with him every step of the way.)

448
00:18:35,818 --> 00:18:37,157
That's so cool.

449
00:18:37,158 --> 00:18:38,388
- It's admirable. - Yes.

450
00:18:38,728 --> 00:18:39,828
It's so admirable.

451
00:18:41,158 --> 00:18:42,228
Let's go.

452
00:18:43,528 --> 00:18:44,798
We can't come back later.

453
00:18:45,368 --> 00:18:48,368
Luckily, it's not raining now. It stopped.

454
00:18:49,138 --> 00:18:51,138
Let's stretch our shoulders and go.

455
00:18:53,608 --> 00:18:55,707
(Stretching before they set out)

456
00:18:55,708 --> 00:18:57,807
My gosh, my shoulders hurt so much. Wait, to the left.

457
00:18:57,808 --> 00:19:00,748
If we don't stretch, our posture gets twisted.

458
00:19:01,178 --> 00:19:02,778
All right. Let's...

459
00:19:03,688 --> 00:19:06,388
- begin another day of walking. - Sung Hwan.

460
00:19:06,588 --> 00:19:08,317
- If we say it's good, it's good. - It's good.

461
00:19:08,318 --> 00:19:10,057
- If we say we can do it, we can. - We can.

462
00:19:10,058 --> 00:19:12,058
- Let's go! - Let's go!

463
00:19:12,428 --> 00:19:13,598
Gosh, that's so cool.

464
00:19:14,328 --> 00:19:15,827
- Let's go. - Let's go.

465
00:19:15,828 --> 00:19:17,298
(They set out at 8am.)

466
00:19:18,328 --> 00:19:21,468
(The two of them are walking to their final destination.)

467
00:19:22,438 --> 00:19:23,708
How do you feel?

468
00:19:24,008 --> 00:19:25,038
I'm just...

469
00:19:26,108 --> 00:19:27,138
Well,

470
00:19:28,338 --> 00:19:29,378
let's try our best.

471
00:19:30,508 --> 00:19:34,118
It might be because it's not raining yet this morning.

472
00:19:35,378 --> 00:19:37,048
I feel great.

473
00:19:37,188 --> 00:19:38,348
It's our last day too.

474
00:19:39,548 --> 00:19:40,857
My gosh, this is great.

475
00:19:40,858 --> 00:19:41,888
(Feeling great)

476
00:19:43,358 --> 00:19:46,457
I'm always in a great mood when we start out.

477
00:19:46,458 --> 00:19:47,527
- Yes. - Yes.

478
00:19:47,528 --> 00:19:49,498
The beginning is always the best part.

479
00:19:50,398 --> 00:19:53,468
I really hope I can continue with this energy level.

480
00:19:53,568 --> 00:19:54,898
(Same here.)

481
00:19:55,768 --> 00:19:58,967
(Fortunately, they feel great at the start of their last day.)

482
00:19:58,968 --> 00:20:00,707
You felt lighter, though. Right?

483
00:20:00,708 --> 00:20:02,278
It was our last day too.

484
00:20:02,408 --> 00:20:04,248
And we were getting close to our destination.

485
00:20:06,278 --> 00:20:07,648
I need to read the map accurately.

486
00:20:10,288 --> 00:20:12,848
(Focused)

487
00:20:14,218 --> 00:20:15,258
This way.

488
00:20:18,528 --> 00:20:19,788
Go straight.

489
00:20:21,228 --> 00:20:24,197
(Thanks to the Walking GPS, they keep walking without worry.)

490
00:20:24,198 --> 00:20:26,398
(Looking reliable)

491
00:20:27,368 --> 00:20:30,708
Gosh, we both love beer.

492
00:20:31,768 --> 00:20:33,337
- You both like to drink. - I see.

493
00:20:33,338 --> 00:20:34,638
We promised each other...

494
00:20:34,978 --> 00:20:37,977
that we wouldn't have a drop of alcohol or overeat.

495
00:20:37,978 --> 00:20:39,047
If we overeat,

496
00:20:39,048 --> 00:20:40,477
- our pace will slow down. - Right.

497
00:20:40,478 --> 00:20:43,218
We tried really hard to keep these two promises.

498
00:20:43,888 --> 00:20:45,447
It's our last day.

499
00:20:45,448 --> 00:20:47,208
What do you want to eat the most after this?

500
00:20:47,858 --> 00:20:49,887
I want fried chicken...

501
00:20:49,888 --> 00:20:51,848
- Me too. I craved that too. - with draft beer...

502
00:20:52,258 --> 00:20:54,027
- and a shot of soju. - Gosh.

503
00:20:54,028 --> 00:20:55,228
He's smiling.

504
00:20:55,298 --> 00:20:56,628
(Giggling)

505
00:20:59,628 --> 00:21:02,698
I also want tteokbokki and sundae.

506
00:21:06,978 --> 00:21:08,007
(Visualizing)

507
00:21:08,008 --> 00:21:09,478
This is like military training.

508
00:21:09,578 --> 00:21:10,954
- It was quite similar to that. - Right.

509
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,978
- I did that too while marching. - Right.

510
00:21:13,378 --> 00:21:14,698
It's just like military training.

511
00:21:15,748 --> 00:21:16,888
I want...

512
00:21:18,288 --> 00:21:19,788
Since we'll be in Busan...

513
00:21:20,218 --> 00:21:22,957
Wait. CO KUN talked about this. What was that?

514
00:21:22,958 --> 00:21:24,728
- What is it? - I really craved it.

515
00:21:24,988 --> 00:21:26,928
Lee Jae Mo Pizza.

516
00:21:27,258 --> 00:21:28,928
- I see. - Pizza.

517
00:21:29,528 --> 00:21:31,128
A can of beer to go with that.

518
00:21:31,568 --> 00:21:33,537
Okay. I love it. Pizza.

519
00:21:33,538 --> 00:21:36,698
(Just thinking about food brings up his appetite.)

520
00:21:37,338 --> 00:21:40,068
You know what? The weather forecast said...

521
00:21:40,508 --> 00:21:43,547
it would rain a lot starting at 7am.

522
00:21:43,548 --> 00:21:45,848
- Yes. - The weather is on our side.

523
00:21:47,248 --> 00:21:49,878
- I hope it stays that way. - So... Yes.

524
00:21:52,248 --> 00:21:54,988
Gosh. It's not raining, though.

525
00:21:55,188 --> 00:21:57,958
The universe is on our side!

526
00:21:58,158 --> 00:21:59,227
It didn't rain.

527
00:21:59,228 --> 00:22:02,358
The forecast said it would rain a lot!

528
00:22:02,628 --> 00:22:04,997
I knew it! The universe is on our side!

529
00:22:04,998 --> 00:22:06,228
It's on our side!

530
00:22:06,368 --> 00:22:07,837
I felt so good.

531
00:22:07,838 --> 00:22:09,467
When you walk in the rain, your feet get wet.

532
00:22:09,468 --> 00:22:10,508
Right.

533
00:22:12,838 --> 00:22:15,438
Hey. We're full of energy in the morning.

534
00:22:15,578 --> 00:22:17,577
- If we say it's good... - It's good!

535
00:22:17,578 --> 00:22:19,977
- If we say we can do it, we can! - We can!

536
00:22:19,978 --> 00:22:22,278
- Let's go! - Let's go!

537
00:22:22,318 --> 00:22:23,987
You guys have excellent teamwork.

538
00:22:23,988 --> 00:22:25,147
We had nothing to talk about.

539
00:22:25,148 --> 00:22:26,688
- We did that for 17 days. - Really?

540
00:22:27,518 --> 00:22:28,518
- Right. - Let's go.

541
00:22:28,519 --> 00:22:31,627
This chant helped us a lot while walking.

542
00:22:31,628 --> 00:22:33,504
- Right. Chants are important. - Yes, they are.

543
00:22:33,528 --> 00:22:34,727
- They help you stay grounded. - Right.

544
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:35,728
So they're important.

545
00:22:36,458 --> 00:22:38,167
(West Nakdong River)

546
00:22:38,168 --> 00:22:41,798
(With their powerful chant they shouted for 17 days, )

547
00:22:42,568 --> 00:22:46,308
(they cheerfully keep marching.)

548
00:22:46,568 --> 00:22:47,838
Gosh, how beautiful.

549
00:22:48,738 --> 00:22:49,908
Oh, my.

550
00:22:50,948 --> 00:22:51,977
(A pink tunnel of cherry blossoms)

551
00:22:51,978 --> 00:22:53,348
- What a nice path. - Gosh.

552
00:22:53,618 --> 00:22:54,848
It's so beautiful.

553
00:22:56,918 --> 00:22:59,688
This always gives me energy when I'm out walking.

554
00:23:00,618 --> 00:23:02,418
When I'm about to get tired,

555
00:23:03,288 --> 00:23:04,958
I see beautiful trails like this.

556
00:23:05,758 --> 00:23:07,128
(Amazed)

557
00:23:07,798 --> 00:23:10,238
This is the exact reason I wanted to walk across the country.

558
00:23:10,628 --> 00:23:12,528
- What a beautiful place. - Yes.

559
00:23:13,598 --> 00:23:16,667
(They walk while enjoying the floral scent.)

560
00:23:16,668 --> 00:23:18,538
I love walking like this.

561
00:23:19,668 --> 00:23:21,038
I mean, even now,

562
00:23:21,138 --> 00:23:23,007
I'm not thinking about anything.

563
00:23:23,008 --> 00:23:24,008
Right.

564
00:23:24,009 --> 00:23:25,808
I have zero thoughts, which is nice.

565
00:23:26,408 --> 00:23:28,847
When will I get a chance to enjoy a beautiful trail like this?

566
00:23:28,848 --> 00:23:31,408
(When will I get a chance to enjoy a beautiful trail like this?)

567
00:23:31,488 --> 00:23:33,408
Look over there. This entire place is beautiful.

568
00:23:35,888 --> 00:23:38,787
(A moment with a breathtaking view including the Nakdong River)

569
00:23:38,788 --> 00:23:41,628
It's definitely less exhausting when the view is nice.

570
00:23:42,058 --> 00:23:43,228
It was so beautiful.

571
00:23:43,928 --> 00:23:45,328
The trail we walked...

572
00:23:45,768 --> 00:23:49,398
Out of all the trails we walked, today's trail...

573
00:23:49,738 --> 00:23:52,338
was the longest one with cherry blossoms.

574
00:23:52,738 --> 00:23:54,177
The cherry blossoms here haven't bloomed yet.

575
00:23:54,178 --> 00:23:55,237
Wait, are they not cherry blossoms?

576
00:23:55,238 --> 00:23:56,607
That was from Day One when we had just begun.

577
00:23:56,608 --> 00:23:57,777
I see. On your first day...

578
00:23:57,778 --> 00:23:59,338
The cherry blossoms hadn't bloomed yet.

579
00:23:59,508 --> 00:24:01,518
Seriously. They look just like popcorn.

580
00:24:01,618 --> 00:24:03,687
- Beautiful, right? - They bloomed gradually.

581
00:24:03,688 --> 00:24:06,388
It gets warmer in the south.

582
00:24:06,618 --> 00:24:08,018
- Flowers bloom early there. - Yes.

583
00:24:08,758 --> 00:24:10,087
They look like popcorn.

584
00:24:10,088 --> 00:24:11,387
(Filmed by Sung Hwan)

585
00:24:11,388 --> 00:24:14,557
The cherry blossoms are welcoming us.

586
00:24:14,558 --> 00:24:15,728
This is nice.

587
00:24:19,098 --> 00:24:20,098
(The most romantic sight on their last day)

588
00:24:20,099 --> 00:24:22,338
Gosh, this trail is just crazy.

589
00:24:22,698 --> 00:24:24,807
This is such a luxury for us. I mean it.

590
00:24:24,808 --> 00:24:27,038
My gosh. It's already become a cherished memory.

591
00:24:28,038 --> 00:24:30,878
(Thanks to that, they're getting into the spring spirit.)

592
00:24:31,148 --> 00:24:32,748
The petals are falling down.

593
00:24:33,848 --> 00:24:36,818
(Getting showered by the petals, the peak of romance)

594
00:24:37,448 --> 00:24:38,618
Seriously.

595
00:24:39,488 --> 00:24:41,718
I'll never forget this moment until the day I die.

596
00:24:45,128 --> 00:24:47,998
(Sung Hwan's journey across the country, filled with romance)

597
00:24:48,958 --> 00:24:50,258
(Sighing)

598
00:24:54,498 --> 00:24:56,438
Gosh, I'm feeling it now.

599
00:24:58,938 --> 00:25:01,498
Forget about the romantic view or whatever. How far did we come?

600
00:25:02,778 --> 00:25:03,847
Only 2km.

601
00:25:03,848 --> 00:25:05,407
- You only walked 2km? - My gosh. Only that?

602
00:25:05,408 --> 00:25:07,817
- Gosh, around that time... - Your energy level dropped so fast.

603
00:25:07,818 --> 00:25:08,947
(His energy level dropped rapidly.)

604
00:25:08,948 --> 00:25:10,118
It's only been 2km.

605
00:25:11,148 --> 00:25:13,688
Our fatigue accumulated. That's why...

606
00:25:14,758 --> 00:25:15,888
we get tired quickly.

607
00:25:16,858 --> 00:25:19,158
It's because of ongoing fatigue, right?

608
00:25:19,228 --> 00:25:21,057
He's been walking at his limit.

609
00:25:21,058 --> 00:25:23,397
- Right. I was at my limit. - He had already hit his limit.

610
00:25:23,398 --> 00:25:25,198
- I hit my limit three days ago. - Right?

611
00:25:27,098 --> 00:25:28,567
(Community Center of Anmak 1-gu to Gwangalli Beach)

612
00:25:28,568 --> 00:25:31,408
(Distance traveled: 2km)

613
00:25:32,638 --> 00:25:34,637
We have a long way to go.

614
00:25:34,638 --> 00:25:35,808
- Gosh. - That's long indeed.

615
00:25:37,108 --> 00:25:38,548
(Glancing)

616
00:25:39,008 --> 00:25:41,278
"Agricultural Technology Center."

617
00:25:42,548 --> 00:25:44,047
(Entering Busan)

618
00:25:44,048 --> 00:25:45,387
- But you guys made it to Busan. - It's Busan.

619
00:25:45,388 --> 00:25:48,187
We slept in Gimhae the night before, and we made it to Busan.

620
00:25:48,188 --> 00:25:49,628
- You guys are getting close. - Yes.

621
00:25:50,218 --> 00:25:52,858
- Is that Gupo? Or the one after? - It's right here.

622
00:25:54,428 --> 00:25:55,828
We'll have to cross it.

623
00:25:57,468 --> 00:26:00,998
(Heading toward Gupo with the Walking GPS' guidance)

624
00:26:02,668 --> 00:26:04,238
Gosh, we have to climb stairs again.

625
00:26:07,638 --> 00:26:09,637
To cross the Gupo Bridge,

626
00:26:09,638 --> 00:26:11,947
we have to climb up the stairs to cross it.

627
00:26:11,948 --> 00:26:13,077
(Trying their best to climb the stairs)

628
00:26:13,078 --> 00:26:15,278
Stairs are the toughest.

629
00:26:17,648 --> 00:26:19,247
- Oh, my. - That's not easy.

630
00:26:19,248 --> 00:26:20,718
- It wasn't easy. - Oh, my.

631
00:26:21,788 --> 00:26:23,587
- If we say it's good, it's good. - It's good.

632
00:26:23,588 --> 00:26:25,757
- If we say we can do it, we can. - We can.

633
00:26:25,758 --> 00:26:28,028
- Let's go. - Let's go.

634
00:26:28,298 --> 00:26:30,428
- Let's go. - Let's go.

635
00:26:31,468 --> 00:26:32,528
Let's go.

636
00:26:32,968 --> 00:26:35,098
- You can't do it without the chant. - Let's go.

637
00:26:35,368 --> 00:26:36,867
- Oh, my knees. - They must bring up their energy.

638
00:26:36,868 --> 00:26:37,937
Let's go.

639
00:26:37,938 --> 00:26:39,467
I know you have bad knees. This is impressive.

640
00:26:39,468 --> 00:26:42,238
Right. It's really hard to walk when your knees hurt.

641
00:26:43,108 --> 00:26:46,708
(Sung Hwan keeps pushing himself despite the unfavorable conditions.)

642
00:26:48,178 --> 00:26:49,747
Sung Hwan, your determination is impressive.

643
00:26:49,748 --> 00:26:51,047
Right. This isn't easy.

644
00:26:51,048 --> 00:26:53,048
- He's so determined. - You're amazing.

645
00:26:54,718 --> 00:26:55,858
Let's go.

646
00:26:58,688 --> 00:27:03,798
(They barely manage to climb up to the Gupo Bridge.)

647
00:27:04,398 --> 00:27:05,567
(Zooming by)

648
00:27:05,568 --> 00:27:07,197
(Swooshing)

649
00:27:07,198 --> 00:27:08,938
(Swishing)

650
00:27:09,198 --> 00:27:10,938
Gosh, it's super windy up here.

651
00:27:11,708 --> 00:27:12,767
(On an elevated bridge...)

652
00:27:12,768 --> 00:27:16,238
It was incredibly windy on the bridge.

653
00:27:16,608 --> 00:27:18,508
I can't keep my eyes open.

654
00:27:20,148 --> 00:27:22,748
The wind was typhoon-level strong.

655
00:27:23,148 --> 00:27:26,888
(Walking for quite a while against the strong wind)

656
00:27:28,688 --> 00:27:31,388
(Exclaiming)

657
00:27:31,628 --> 00:27:35,098
(Frowning)

658
00:27:35,798 --> 00:27:37,297
- Oh, gosh. - What is it?

659
00:27:37,298 --> 00:27:39,628
(Sung Hwan's face twists more and more.)

660
00:27:40,498 --> 00:27:42,538
(Fidgety)

661
00:27:43,138 --> 00:27:44,767
- Oh, gosh. - What is it?

662
00:27:44,768 --> 00:27:45,768
(Sung Hwan seems to feel uncomfortable...)

663
00:27:45,769 --> 00:27:46,808
(on top of Gupo Bridge.)

664
00:27:47,808 --> 00:27:50,108
(Fidgety)

665
00:27:51,008 --> 00:27:53,008
- I need to use the restroom. - Okay.

666
00:27:53,378 --> 00:27:54,977
- A gas station or... - Oh, his stomach hurts.

667
00:27:54,978 --> 00:27:56,418
I need to... My gosh.

668
00:27:57,748 --> 00:27:58,947
He ate too much.

669
00:27:58,948 --> 00:28:01,788
(Was my breakfast too hearty?)

670
00:28:03,018 --> 00:28:04,557
Gosh, there's no restroom...

671
00:28:04,558 --> 00:28:06,678
on the cross-country track. This is driving me crazy.

672
00:28:08,958 --> 00:28:10,227
(Quickly looking for the restroom)

673
00:28:10,228 --> 00:28:12,268
- He's looking for the restroom. - This is serious.

674
00:28:12,468 --> 00:28:14,367
There's a 911 rescue center.

675
00:28:14,368 --> 00:28:16,008
- When we go down? - Yes, let's go there.

676
00:28:17,338 --> 00:28:18,867
I think we're around 500m or 600m away.

677
00:28:18,868 --> 00:28:20,984
(He'll use the restroom of the rescue center under the bridge.)

678
00:28:21,008 --> 00:28:22,708
I might end up in big trouble.

679
00:28:23,138 --> 00:28:24,408
Back then, I was...

680
00:28:24,848 --> 00:28:26,278
Why is the bridge so long?

681
00:28:27,278 --> 00:28:28,677
Gosh, I'm dying to poop.

682
00:28:28,678 --> 00:28:30,347
(I'm dying to poop.)

683
00:28:30,348 --> 00:28:31,588
You're so instinct-driven.

684
00:28:31,788 --> 00:28:33,588
I had it really hard then.

685
00:28:34,518 --> 00:28:35,518
My goodness.

686
00:28:35,519 --> 00:28:36,918
(Halting)

687
00:28:37,258 --> 00:28:38,688
Gosh, this is serious.

688
00:28:40,228 --> 00:28:41,428
Goodness, what do I do?

689
00:28:41,698 --> 00:28:43,828
It was really hard then. It was a crisis.

690
00:28:44,498 --> 00:28:46,797
Gosh, there's no restroom on the cross-country track.

691
00:28:46,798 --> 00:28:48,744
- This is driving me crazy. - There's no restroom.

692
00:28:48,768 --> 00:28:52,838
Those who have done a cross-country walk must know.

693
00:28:53,168 --> 00:28:54,578
Going to a restroom...

694
00:28:55,908 --> 00:28:57,948
- is troublesome. - It must not be easy.

695
00:28:58,078 --> 00:29:01,717
There are times when there aren't any convenience stores within 10km.

696
00:29:01,718 --> 00:29:03,577
- What do you do then? - It's really hard to find one...

697
00:29:03,578 --> 00:29:05,258
- once you're out of city. - You're right.

698
00:29:05,788 --> 00:29:07,118
That must be the worst.

699
00:29:07,618 --> 00:29:09,118
(Worried)

700
00:29:09,818 --> 00:29:10,988
Do we have about 300m to go?

701
00:29:11,528 --> 00:29:13,888
We have around 300m to go. We can go down this way.

702
00:29:14,698 --> 00:29:15,997
It was really hard then.

703
00:29:15,998 --> 00:29:17,927
(He's on the verge of crying.)

704
00:29:17,928 --> 00:29:20,197
- Oh, gosh. - You should minimize moving.

705
00:29:20,198 --> 00:29:22,278
That's right. You should shake your upper body less.

706
00:29:22,698 --> 00:29:23,698
My gosh.

707
00:29:23,868 --> 00:29:26,508
Gosh, this is really serious.

708
00:29:27,008 --> 00:29:28,608
The poop is almost hanging.

709
00:29:29,338 --> 00:29:30,338
What did he say?

710
00:29:31,008 --> 00:29:34,218
Sung Hwan is walking while clenching his anus.

711
00:29:35,018 --> 00:29:36,018
Seriously...

712
00:29:36,019 --> 00:29:38,087
But your bow-legged walking is fixed.

713
00:29:38,088 --> 00:29:40,188
(Thanks to that, his bow-legged walking is fixed.)

714
00:29:40,688 --> 00:29:43,408
(His unrivaled bow-legged walking he's been keeping for a long time)

715
00:29:44,058 --> 00:29:45,058
That's good.

716
00:29:47,928 --> 00:29:49,058
Gosh, my stomach hurts.

717
00:29:50,798 --> 00:29:51,867
He's almost there.

718
00:29:51,868 --> 00:29:53,548
(He can slowly see the end of the bridge.)

719
00:29:55,838 --> 00:29:57,307
(But hold on.)

720
00:29:57,308 --> 00:29:58,908
It came out.

721
00:29:59,268 --> 00:30:03,108
(The 2nd stomach issue)

722
00:30:03,608 --> 00:30:04,708
How much longer to go?

723
00:30:05,878 --> 00:30:07,648
It's right below. Let's go.

724
00:30:11,388 --> 00:30:12,948
Gosh, I should get ready.

725
00:30:15,118 --> 00:30:16,157
Open it.

726
00:30:16,158 --> 00:30:17,158
That's right.

727
00:30:17,159 --> 00:30:19,440
- You should get ready in advance. - Yes, it's important.

728
00:30:20,858 --> 00:30:22,057
He should go as soon as he opens the door.

729
00:30:22,058 --> 00:30:23,058
It's open.

730
00:30:24,098 --> 00:30:26,527
Hongga, please take this in advance.

731
00:30:26,528 --> 00:30:27,538
This won't do.

732
00:30:27,838 --> 00:30:30,138
Hongga did so many things.

733
00:30:31,968 --> 00:30:33,067
(Taking each step carefully)

734
00:30:33,068 --> 00:30:34,238
It's tough when you go down.

735
00:30:37,408 --> 00:30:38,777
(911 Rescue Center)

736
00:30:38,778 --> 00:30:40,678
It really is an emergency.

737
00:30:45,318 --> 00:30:47,788
(Finally, )

738
00:30:48,858 --> 00:30:51,728
(Sung Hwan is rescued.)

739
00:30:52,758 --> 00:30:54,258
Thank you. I almost died.

740
00:30:55,928 --> 00:30:58,497
- I almost died. - You feel ecstatic then.

741
00:30:58,498 --> 00:30:59,567
Thank you so much.

742
00:30:59,568 --> 00:31:01,008
- Not at all. - You're my lifesaver.

743
00:31:01,298 --> 00:31:02,998
- Thank you. I'm off. - Bye.

744
00:31:03,638 --> 00:31:05,758
I'll drop by to say hello next time when I'm in town.

745
00:31:07,738 --> 00:31:09,007
(I feel better now.)

746
00:31:09,008 --> 00:31:10,178
He looks more relaxed.

747
00:31:12,108 --> 00:31:13,608
- Hongga. - Yes?

748
00:31:13,748 --> 00:31:16,178
Happiness is right beside you, not somewhere far.

749
00:31:17,488 --> 00:31:19,494
This is something so small, but it makes me so happy.

750
00:31:19,518 --> 00:31:20,817
He's learning about life.

751
00:31:20,818 --> 00:31:22,058
I almost died.

752
00:31:23,958 --> 00:31:25,758
It's full-on downtown from here.

753
00:31:27,528 --> 00:31:31,267
(They reach the city center after crossing Gupo Bridge.)

754
00:31:31,268 --> 00:31:32,468
Yes, from now...

755
00:31:33,698 --> 00:31:35,268
I want to drink something cold.

756
00:31:35,638 --> 00:31:36,698
Right.

757
00:31:37,138 --> 00:31:40,007
For eight days, we only walked country roads.

758
00:31:40,008 --> 00:31:41,137
It was our first time...

759
00:31:41,138 --> 00:31:42,498
- seeing the city center. - Right.

760
00:31:42,908 --> 00:31:44,428
You must've been glad to see the city.

761
00:31:47,278 --> 00:31:48,378
Where are they?

762
00:31:48,818 --> 00:31:49,977
(After walking through the alley, an overpass shows up.)

763
00:31:49,978 --> 00:31:51,017
- It's an overpass. - Yes.

764
00:31:51,018 --> 00:31:52,088
The overpass is...

765
00:31:52,148 --> 00:31:53,787
As we walked, we realized...

766
00:31:53,788 --> 00:31:55,388
there were so many overpasses in Korea.

767
00:31:56,818 --> 00:31:58,427
(They start climbing up the stairs.)

768
00:31:58,428 --> 00:31:59,428
Goodness.

769
00:32:00,958 --> 00:32:03,228
(Sighing)

770
00:32:04,228 --> 00:32:05,797
(He's exhausted as soon as he starts climbing.)

771
00:32:05,798 --> 00:32:06,798
All right.

772
00:32:07,438 --> 00:32:10,298
(Where did his bright smile from a moment ago go?)

773
00:32:11,568 --> 00:32:13,637
(His smile disappeared in an instant.)

774
00:32:13,638 --> 00:32:14,638
All right.

775
00:32:14,808 --> 00:32:18,807
(Sighing)

776
00:32:18,808 --> 00:32:20,168
Your knees must've been destroyed.

777
00:32:21,348 --> 00:32:24,288
(He crossed the overpass with difficulty.)

778
00:32:25,948 --> 00:32:27,718
(Breathing out)

779
00:32:28,818 --> 00:32:32,388
(Soon, they start going uphill.)

780
00:32:32,958 --> 00:32:35,758
(Sighing)

781
00:32:37,158 --> 00:32:38,798
The apple we had last time...

782
00:32:39,598 --> 00:32:40,997
- and strawberries. - Strawberries.

783
00:32:40,998 --> 00:32:42,297
(As he's exhausted, he thinks of fruits.)

784
00:32:42,298 --> 00:32:43,498
I suddenly crave those.

785
00:32:44,638 --> 00:32:45,867
- They must be low on sugar. - Here...

786
00:32:45,868 --> 00:32:47,368
(I crave something sweet.)

787
00:32:48,308 --> 00:32:50,778
(The uphill road continues.)

788
00:32:51,978 --> 00:32:53,078
Gosh, my legs.

789
00:32:53,878 --> 00:32:55,048
My knees hurt too.

790
00:32:56,178 --> 00:32:57,178
(Panting)

791
00:32:58,418 --> 00:32:59,418
(Panting)

792
00:32:59,518 --> 00:33:01,317
An uphill road is really tough.

793
00:33:01,318 --> 00:33:03,818
- Hongga didn't say a word. - Turn right here.

794
00:33:03,988 --> 00:33:05,088
He's amazing.

795
00:33:06,628 --> 00:33:07,727
Gosh, my legs.

796
00:33:07,728 --> 00:33:10,598
(He continues to go forward with Hongga who's been quiet.)

797
00:33:10,968 --> 00:33:12,828
How are the tangerines so beautiful?

798
00:33:13,568 --> 00:33:15,237
Gosh, this is no joke!

799
00:33:15,238 --> 00:33:16,938
(It's a fruit store!)

800
00:33:17,568 --> 00:33:19,008
My hands are shaking!

801
00:33:19,708 --> 00:33:20,738
Thank you.

802
00:33:20,908 --> 00:33:22,337
(Suddenly getting excited upon seeing fruits on the way)

803
00:33:22,338 --> 00:33:23,408
Gosh, I'm so tired.

804
00:33:23,808 --> 00:33:25,407
As soon as we talked about fruits,

805
00:33:25,408 --> 00:33:27,978
we came into a fruit alley.

806
00:33:28,578 --> 00:33:30,917
What is this? They're all fruit stores.

807
00:33:30,918 --> 00:33:32,988
We just talked about fruits.

808
00:33:34,818 --> 00:33:36,187
What kind of apple is this?

809
00:33:36,188 --> 00:33:37,988
- I shouldn't look. - That's green apple.

810
00:33:39,858 --> 00:33:42,098
- It's Korean beef. - You just walked past it?

811
00:33:42,698 --> 00:33:45,198
- You could eat 1. - You could've eaten 1.

812
00:33:45,468 --> 00:33:46,997
I was going to eat during a break.

813
00:33:46,998 --> 00:33:49,398
- He had to eat during a break. - He planned out a routine.

814
00:33:49,938 --> 00:33:52,767
It's more difficult in the city.

815
00:33:52,768 --> 00:33:54,338
You didn't eat while walking.

816
00:33:54,838 --> 00:33:55,878
Gosh, look at that.

817
00:33:56,078 --> 00:33:57,918
Old-style jjajangmyeon. Machine-made milmyeon.

818
00:33:58,108 --> 00:34:00,077
The sign that says Chinese food is all ripped.

819
00:34:00,078 --> 00:34:01,477
(Fancy restaurants that tempt Sung Hwan)

820
00:34:01,478 --> 00:34:03,218
I can smell Busan in the air.

821
00:34:03,648 --> 00:34:05,588
Gosh, it's making me hungry.

822
00:34:05,848 --> 00:34:07,688
He must be dying to have gukbap.

823
00:34:08,258 --> 00:34:10,688
- You love snacking. - I love it.

824
00:34:11,658 --> 00:34:12,757
Hello.

825
00:34:12,758 --> 00:34:14,897
- Hello. - Hi.

826
00:34:14,898 --> 00:34:15,998
Yes, hello.

827
00:34:16,628 --> 00:34:18,767
- Gosh, ma'am. - Oh, my. You're thin.

828
00:34:18,768 --> 00:34:20,197
I'm thinner than you thought, right?

829
00:34:20,198 --> 00:34:21,837
You became thinner.

830
00:34:21,838 --> 00:34:22,898
Right.

831
00:34:23,098 --> 00:34:24,837
- Yes. - You're so handsome.

832
00:34:24,838 --> 00:34:26,508
- My lady. - Your face is so thin.

833
00:34:26,738 --> 00:34:27,808
Oh, my.

834
00:34:28,278 --> 00:34:30,077
- How come your face is so thin? - It's her first time seeing him.

835
00:34:30,078 --> 00:34:31,407
You're so thin.

836
00:34:31,408 --> 00:34:33,178
- Your face is so thin. - Let's go.

837
00:34:34,418 --> 00:34:37,078
Wait, ma'am! I'm sorry, but you look like me a little.

838
00:34:37,378 --> 00:34:39,048
I've found my mom.

839
00:34:39,788 --> 00:34:41,088
Mom!

840
00:34:41,718 --> 00:34:43,887
- Mom! - Your smile resembles hers.

841
00:34:43,888 --> 00:34:44,928
I'll get going.

842
00:34:45,588 --> 00:34:47,387
- I'll get going. - All right. Have a good one.

843
00:34:47,388 --> 00:34:49,027
- I won't go far to see you off. - Bye!

844
00:34:49,028 --> 00:34:50,227
(Setting off after getting cheered on by the ladies...)

845
00:34:50,228 --> 00:34:51,228
(instead of snacking)

846
00:34:52,368 --> 00:34:53,698
It really cheered me on.

847
00:34:57,168 --> 00:34:59,768
I got cheered on a lot,

848
00:35:00,308 --> 00:35:01,938
- and it helped a lot. - Of course.

849
00:35:05,748 --> 00:35:07,107
(So far, they've walked 8.5km.)

850
00:35:07,108 --> 00:35:08,118
You've come quite far.

851
00:35:09,918 --> 00:35:11,017
They've come a third of the way.

852
00:35:11,018 --> 00:35:13,188
(Remaining distance: 16.5km)

853
00:35:14,458 --> 00:35:17,728
(Going forward quietly)

854
00:35:20,628 --> 00:35:21,958
Gosh, the rain...

855
00:35:23,798 --> 00:35:25,227
Please don't rain.

856
00:35:25,228 --> 00:35:26,367
(Rain slowly starts to fall.)

857
00:35:26,368 --> 00:35:27,568
What's wrong with you?

858
00:35:31,138 --> 00:35:34,138
Since I was wet anyway, I let myself get soaked comfortably.

859
00:35:34,908 --> 00:35:37,278
(This is fun!)

860
00:35:37,678 --> 00:35:39,748
(What's so fun about it?)

861
00:35:40,148 --> 00:35:42,048
He must not talk much except when he raps.

862
00:35:43,718 --> 00:35:45,048
It won't rain more than this.

863
00:35:45,188 --> 00:35:46,918
It's a passing shower.

864
00:35:47,658 --> 00:35:48,858
For a weather fairy like me,

865
00:35:49,588 --> 00:35:51,728
this is all I get.

866
00:35:52,428 --> 00:35:53,988
We can enjoy this much of rain.

867
00:35:54,288 --> 00:35:58,368
(Boom)

868
00:35:58,598 --> 00:36:01,868
(The sky suddenly turns wild.)

869
00:36:02,838 --> 00:36:04,337
Oh, no.

870
00:36:04,338 --> 00:36:06,637
- What bad timing. - As soon as I said that...

871
00:36:06,638 --> 00:36:07,737
It's the same sound...

872
00:36:07,738 --> 00:36:08,738
- from the 911 rescue center. - Exactly.

873
00:36:08,739 --> 00:36:10,538
(Embarrassed)

874
00:36:11,208 --> 00:36:13,108
Please don't be mad. I was just saying it.

875
00:36:14,008 --> 00:36:15,848
(Calm down.)

876
00:36:16,418 --> 00:36:18,048
(Calming down the enraged sky)

877
00:36:18,848 --> 00:36:21,558
(The place they reached after walking for a while)

878
00:36:22,318 --> 00:36:24,057
That's... Gosh, look how good it looks.

879
00:36:24,058 --> 00:36:25,258
Fresh mango bingsu.

880
00:36:25,688 --> 00:36:26,757
Bingsu?

881
00:36:26,758 --> 00:36:27,958
(Fresh mango bingsu)

882
00:36:28,128 --> 00:36:30,028
- When you're low on sugar... - Inhale it!

883
00:36:32,298 --> 00:36:33,897
I'm a bit wet. I'm sorry.

884
00:36:33,898 --> 00:36:35,498
(They enter the place to inhale bingsu.)

885
00:36:36,298 --> 00:36:37,938
We have one snack time.

886
00:36:38,168 --> 00:36:40,868
If the final destination of the day is 26km away...

887
00:36:41,038 --> 00:36:43,078
and a cafe is located at a 15-km point,

888
00:36:43,338 --> 00:36:45,908
we go to that cafe and rest for an hour.

889
00:36:46,578 --> 00:36:49,618
Eating carbs makes us tired,

890
00:36:49,748 --> 00:36:52,648
so we always eat a shake or bingsu.

891
00:36:52,748 --> 00:36:54,518
We eat sugary treats our bodies can absorb.

892
00:36:55,118 --> 00:36:57,518
There aren't many places where we can rest,

893
00:36:57,688 --> 00:36:59,158
so we decide on...

894
00:36:59,458 --> 00:37:01,898
what to eat the day before.

895
00:37:02,328 --> 00:37:05,798
That makes sense. That could change the route.

896
00:37:06,568 --> 00:37:07,968
I wrote that the day before.

897
00:37:09,098 --> 00:37:11,938
- Is that the mango bingsu? - Yes.

898
00:37:13,008 --> 00:37:14,408
I'll order one. I'll order this.

899
00:37:15,138 --> 00:37:17,178
- I'll order patbingsu. - One fresh mango bingsu...

900
00:37:17,208 --> 00:37:18,608
and one patbingsu?

901
00:37:19,178 --> 00:37:22,118
(They go to the table after ordering bingsu.)

902
00:37:23,248 --> 00:37:25,888
(His body aches.)

903
00:37:26,048 --> 00:37:28,018
He struggles to sit.

904
00:37:28,858 --> 00:37:29,918
My goodness.

905
00:37:32,358 --> 00:37:34,628
(Dazed)

906
00:37:34,958 --> 00:37:37,157
(Dazed)

907
00:37:37,158 --> 00:37:38,728
- Hold on. - Their eyes are unfocused.

908
00:37:39,798 --> 00:37:40,927
It's like a mirror.

909
00:37:40,928 --> 00:37:43,568
(It's like a mirror.)

910
00:37:43,738 --> 00:37:45,838
How many kilometers have we traveled?

911
00:37:46,208 --> 00:37:49,438
- We've traveled 11km. - Did you say 11km?

912
00:37:49,838 --> 00:37:52,977
That means we have 14km left to go.

913
00:37:52,978 --> 00:37:54,107
(The remaining distance is 14km.)

914
00:37:54,108 --> 00:37:56,448
I'm so low on sugar.

915
00:37:57,178 --> 00:38:00,148
(He feels dizzy.)

916
00:38:00,518 --> 00:38:02,188
The bingsu you've ordered is ready.

917
00:38:02,418 --> 00:38:05,158
(Finally!)

918
00:38:06,458 --> 00:38:07,727
(Bingsu enters.)

919
00:38:07,728 --> 00:38:08,798
Ma'am.

920
00:38:08,928 --> 00:38:10,328
The bingsu you've ordered is ready.

921
00:38:10,628 --> 00:38:12,298
Ma'am. Thank you.

922
00:38:12,528 --> 00:38:13,598
Here.

923
00:38:13,828 --> 00:38:15,798
- Let's share. - Shall we do that?

924
00:38:15,938 --> 00:38:17,637
- That's insane. - We can scoop out some.

925
00:38:17,638 --> 00:38:18,838
Okay.

926
00:38:18,968 --> 00:38:20,538
- It looks tasty. - I prefer patbingsu.

927
00:38:21,278 --> 00:38:22,308
It looks good.

928
00:38:23,738 --> 00:38:24,808
Look at this mango.

929
00:38:25,478 --> 00:38:27,578
(Appetizing)

930
00:38:28,518 --> 00:38:29,677
(Gasping)

931
00:38:29,678 --> 00:38:30,947
I usually don't like fruits.

932
00:38:30,948 --> 00:38:33,518
(I usually don't like fruits.)

933
00:38:34,918 --> 00:38:37,988
(I love fruits.)

934
00:38:39,188 --> 00:38:42,457
Gosh, look at this. This makes me eat a lot of mangoes.

935
00:38:42,458 --> 00:38:43,498
(Eating)

936
00:38:45,898 --> 00:38:47,658
- His face lit up right away. - My goodness.

937
00:38:47,998 --> 00:38:49,968
(His skin looked dull since he was low on sugar.)

938
00:38:50,738 --> 00:38:53,207
His face suddenly lit up.

939
00:38:53,208 --> 00:38:54,777
(His skin is glowing thanks to bingsu.)

940
00:38:54,778 --> 00:38:56,578
It really raises my blood sugar.

941
00:38:57,638 --> 00:38:59,847
It spread through my veins.

942
00:38:59,848 --> 00:39:01,168
- How fascinating! - My goodness.

943
00:39:01,578 --> 00:39:04,248
(Hongga quickly raises his blood sugar as well.)

944
00:39:04,988 --> 00:39:06,588
- It looks like bibimbap. - I know.

945
00:39:07,548 --> 00:39:08,758
Didn't your teeth feel cold?

946
00:39:09,418 --> 00:39:11,498
They did, but I kept eating because it was so tasty.

947
00:39:12,788 --> 00:39:14,158
He'll go to the 911 center again.

948
00:39:14,288 --> 00:39:16,158
(Watch out for a stomachache.)

949
00:39:16,798 --> 00:39:19,267
Any snack would've tasted good at that point, right?

950
00:39:19,268 --> 00:39:20,527
(A snack break that's as good as a feast)

951
00:39:20,528 --> 00:39:21,598
(His mouth waters.)

952
00:39:22,038 --> 00:39:23,398
I can breathe more easily now.

953
00:39:24,268 --> 00:39:26,108
(It washed away his fatigue.)

954
00:39:27,638 --> 00:39:29,398
What are you going to do with that forehead?

955
00:39:32,048 --> 00:39:34,177
- Didn't he apply sunscreen? - He did.

956
00:39:34,178 --> 00:39:36,258
That day, the sun wasn't so bad because of the rain.

957
00:39:37,178 --> 00:39:39,548
How will you function...

958
00:39:40,288 --> 00:39:41,317
in society?

959
00:39:41,318 --> 00:39:42,558
(Sighing)

960
00:39:43,088 --> 00:39:45,258
(Let's see.)

961
00:39:45,858 --> 00:39:47,997
(Staring)

962
00:39:47,998 --> 00:39:49,558
I guess it's pretty bad.

963
00:39:51,768 --> 00:39:52,828
Oh, no.

964
00:39:53,598 --> 00:39:54,867
For now...

965
00:39:54,868 --> 00:39:55,968
(Upset)

966
00:39:56,538 --> 00:39:58,738
To be honest, I'm so exhausted and weary.

967
00:40:00,868 --> 00:40:03,337
Even if we're tired... If we say it's good,

968
00:40:03,338 --> 00:40:04,338
- it's good. - It's good.

969
00:40:04,339 --> 00:40:05,477
If we say we can do it...

970
00:40:05,478 --> 00:40:08,148
- We can. Let's go! - Let's go!

971
00:40:09,078 --> 00:40:10,978
- They're a positive duo. - I know.

972
00:40:11,388 --> 00:40:12,818
They don't even complain.

973
00:40:14,518 --> 00:40:15,587
(Distance traveled: 11km Distance remaining: 14km)

974
00:40:15,588 --> 00:40:16,787
Be careful.

975
00:40:16,788 --> 00:40:20,558
(Distance traveled: 11km Distance remaining: 14km)

976
00:40:21,058 --> 00:40:24,028
They ate bingsu on a rainy day.

977
00:40:25,428 --> 00:40:26,798
Hey, this route is strange.

978
00:40:26,998 --> 00:40:28,038
Why?

979
00:40:28,198 --> 00:40:29,298
A tunnel?

980
00:40:31,368 --> 00:40:34,537
Busan has so many interesting paths.

981
00:40:34,538 --> 00:40:35,607
Oh, my. How is there...

982
00:40:35,608 --> 00:40:37,407
- What? - such a narrow tunnel?

983
00:40:37,408 --> 00:40:38,578
- What's this? - What?

984
00:40:38,678 --> 00:40:40,778
I would never go in there when I'm running.

985
00:40:41,848 --> 00:40:43,178
(Looking around)

986
00:40:43,478 --> 00:40:46,088
It's a cave.

987
00:40:47,188 --> 00:40:48,817
That tunnel looks cool.

988
00:40:48,818 --> 00:40:50,718
- It's like a mystery spot. - How fascinating.

989
00:40:51,158 --> 00:40:54,028
Hongga should film a music video inside the tunnel.

990
00:40:54,628 --> 00:40:55,997
He had the exact same thought.

991
00:40:55,998 --> 00:40:57,574
- Right? - He wanted to do that next time.

992
00:40:57,598 --> 00:41:00,168
Rappers lose it when they see a tunnel.

993
00:41:01,098 --> 00:41:02,898
- Why do they lose it? - Really?

994
00:41:03,498 --> 00:41:05,307
- They want to rap right away. - Do they want to do this?

995
00:41:05,308 --> 00:41:07,148
Do rappers get excited when they see a tunnel?

996
00:41:07,438 --> 00:41:10,138
When they see a cool tunnel, they think of a camera first.

997
00:41:12,208 --> 00:41:14,448
All of the old music videos were filmed inside a tunnel.

998
00:41:14,678 --> 00:41:17,078
- And that tunnel is unique. - Right.

999
00:41:17,448 --> 00:41:19,448
He must have been excited walking there.

1000
00:41:22,318 --> 00:41:23,618
Is that rain?

1001
00:41:24,728 --> 00:41:26,027
It's raining hard.

1002
00:41:26,028 --> 00:41:27,628
(Rain has turned heavier.)

1003
00:41:28,898 --> 00:41:30,998
Gosh, even the weather is...

1004
00:41:31,828 --> 00:41:33,128
on our side.

1005
00:41:36,838 --> 00:41:38,568
You could slip in the rain.

1006
00:41:38,768 --> 00:41:40,868
Since it rained a lot, the road was very slippery.

1007
00:41:45,378 --> 00:41:47,098
Still, it's nice to do this on a rainy day.

1008
00:41:49,518 --> 00:41:50,648
Rain harder!

1009
00:41:52,018 --> 00:41:55,158
(Grimacing)

1010
00:41:55,318 --> 00:41:57,418
Hongga is more expressive than most actors.

1011
00:41:57,988 --> 00:42:00,187
- He doesn't even need to talk. - No.

1012
00:42:00,188 --> 00:42:01,328
He speaks with his face.

1013
00:42:02,058 --> 00:42:03,528
(I'm impressed.)

1014
00:42:04,258 --> 00:42:06,868
(They can barely open their eyes because of the rain.)

1015
00:42:08,438 --> 00:42:09,497
My goodness.

1016
00:42:09,498 --> 00:42:10,697
(But they keep walking toward the Gwangalli Beach.)

1017
00:42:10,698 --> 00:42:12,938
Even the weather helps our festival.

1018
00:42:17,708 --> 00:42:19,148
Gosh, it's scary.

1019
00:42:21,378 --> 00:42:25,548
(At the end of the fear-filled gaze)

1020
00:42:25,918 --> 00:42:27,488
- Is that it? - It's this way.

1021
00:42:29,018 --> 00:42:30,817
(An uphill road appears.)

1022
00:42:30,818 --> 00:42:32,057
I hate an uphill road.

1023
00:42:32,058 --> 00:42:34,158
Stairs are better.

1024
00:42:35,858 --> 00:42:38,728
(They meet an uphill road after walking about 430km.)

1025
00:42:40,228 --> 00:42:42,338
(Grunting)

1026
00:42:43,138 --> 00:42:46,738
(Hold on.)

1027
00:42:47,468 --> 00:42:49,078
This hill is intense.

1028
00:42:49,278 --> 00:42:50,708
What's that?

1029
00:42:51,408 --> 00:42:54,048
(He becomes speechless.)

1030
00:42:54,678 --> 00:42:55,747
Is there another one?

1031
00:42:55,748 --> 00:42:57,478
This isn't a hill, but a mountain.

1032
00:42:57,848 --> 00:42:59,687
Sung Hwan usually doesn't take...

1033
00:42:59,688 --> 00:43:01,488
- an uphill road. - I know.

1034
00:43:02,158 --> 00:43:03,918
So it'll be hard on his calves and glutes.

1035
00:43:04,258 --> 00:43:06,828
(Panting)

1036
00:43:08,158 --> 00:43:10,197
- The uphill continues. - It continues.

1037
00:43:10,198 --> 00:43:11,427
It's almost a mountain.

1038
00:43:11,428 --> 00:43:13,868
(Their feet become heavy.)

1039
00:43:17,698 --> 00:43:20,268
(He hangs his head.)

1040
00:43:21,338 --> 00:43:23,277
It's seriously steep.

1041
00:43:23,278 --> 00:43:24,407
(The boss-level uphill road appears.)

1042
00:43:24,408 --> 00:43:26,347
- Go on. I'll follow you. - Come on, Sung Hwan.

1043
00:43:26,348 --> 00:43:27,788
(Go on without me. I'll follow you.)

1044
