1298
00:54:18,768 --> 00:54:21,127
Tell me where it needs to be set up first.

1299
00:54:21,128 --> 00:54:23,238
Oh, right. This way.

1300
00:54:23,638 --> 00:54:24,868
I want to place it here.

1301
00:54:25,608 --> 00:54:26,808
- Like this? - Yes.

1302
00:54:27,168 --> 00:54:28,778
- I'll clean this up quickly. - Okay.

1303
00:54:28,908 --> 00:54:30,778
- I'll bring it up. - Okay.

1304
00:54:32,978 --> 00:54:34,348
- What is that? - What is that?

1305
00:54:35,848 --> 00:54:37,848
I had this dream ever since I was a kid.

1306
00:54:38,548 --> 00:54:40,118
"What if I had a bunk bed?"

1307
00:54:40,218 --> 00:54:41,487
- What? - In that house?

1308
00:54:41,488 --> 00:54:42,517
I had this dream ever since I was a kid.

1309
00:54:42,518 --> 00:54:44,188
A bed instead of a partition?

1310
00:54:44,488 --> 00:54:45,527
Right.

1311
00:54:45,528 --> 00:54:47,527
- Hold on. It's 19 square meters. - A bunk bed?

1312
00:54:47,528 --> 00:54:49,027
A bunk bed in a place that big?

1313
00:54:49,028 --> 00:54:51,198
- That will fill up the whole place. - Right.

1314
00:54:51,758 --> 00:54:54,467
I had a lot of things I wanted to do...

1315
00:54:54,468 --> 00:54:56,137
when living alone.

1316
00:54:56,138 --> 00:54:58,037
I'm making them happen 1 by 1.

1317
00:54:58,038 --> 00:55:00,567
I wanted to utilize the space of the first floor of the bunk bed.

1318
00:55:00,568 --> 00:55:01,568
Just like that.

1319
00:55:01,569 --> 00:55:03,778
- Right. - I felt I would be really happy...

1320
00:55:04,338 --> 00:55:06,478
by doing this.

1321
00:55:06,648 --> 00:55:09,178
That was why I made a big decision to purchase a bunk bed.

1322
00:55:09,918 --> 00:55:11,677
This should be moved first.

1323
00:55:11,678 --> 00:55:12,947
- I'll clean this up quickly. - Okay.

1324
00:55:12,948 --> 00:55:14,918
- I'll bring it up. - Okay.

1325
00:55:15,958 --> 00:55:17,488
(Flapping)

1326
00:55:17,688 --> 00:55:19,257
(She starts making urgent steps.)

1327
00:55:19,258 --> 00:55:20,688
What should I wear?

1328
00:55:21,288 --> 00:55:22,574
- Hurry. - Check out the clapping.

1329
00:55:22,598 --> 00:55:23,598
Here.

1330
00:55:23,599 --> 00:55:26,098
(She picks her clothes without delay.)

1331
00:55:27,168 --> 00:55:28,168
(Brushing)

1332
00:55:28,169 --> 00:55:29,437
Oh, no!

1333
00:55:29,438 --> 00:55:31,198
That will make your gums bleed. Gosh!

1334
00:55:31,768 --> 00:55:36,208
The installer came faster than the appointed time.

1335
00:55:36,308 --> 00:55:37,707
I had dried laver earlier.

1336
00:55:37,708 --> 00:55:39,948
- It's to keep her manners. - Right.

1337
00:55:41,108 --> 00:55:44,148
(She brushes her teeth at full speed to remove the dried laver.)

1338
00:55:45,448 --> 00:55:46,747
Gosh, she's in a hurry.

1339
00:55:46,748 --> 00:55:49,788
(Her extreme anxiousness cannot be hidden.)

1340
00:55:50,488 --> 00:55:54,758
(She starts cleaning after getting changed.)

1341
00:55:55,928 --> 00:55:56,958
Gosh.

1342
00:55:58,528 --> 00:56:00,867
(She gets things moved diligently while panting.)

1343
00:56:00,868 --> 00:56:02,567
She must be really diligent.

1344
00:56:02,568 --> 00:56:04,037
She's really quick with her actions.

1345
00:56:04,038 --> 00:56:06,207
- She's so fast. - She's always really fast.

1346
00:56:06,208 --> 00:56:07,608
(Rushing)

1347
00:56:09,538 --> 00:56:10,538
(Throwing)

1348
00:56:10,878 --> 00:56:12,277
(Her abandoned sock gets thrown into a corner.)

1349
00:56:12,278 --> 00:56:13,878
(There we go!)

1350
00:56:15,248 --> 00:56:18,048
(She moves quickly to place the rug.)

1351
00:56:18,818 --> 00:56:19,848
Okay.

1352
00:56:20,188 --> 00:56:21,188
Gosh.

1353
00:56:22,688 --> 00:56:24,087
- Sir. - Yes?

1354
00:56:24,088 --> 00:56:25,487
I moved everything.

1355
00:56:25,488 --> 00:56:26,957
I tried my best to pretend not to be out of breath.

1356
00:56:26,958 --> 00:56:28,058
"Sir."

1357
00:56:31,028 --> 00:56:32,127
(She crouches in the corner.)

1358
00:56:32,128 --> 00:56:34,067
- On top of the rug, right? - Yes.

1359
00:56:34,068 --> 00:56:35,367
(She's taking a breather while crouching on the floor.)

1360
00:56:35,368 --> 00:56:36,608
She's sitting there like a cat.

1361
00:56:37,638 --> 00:56:40,337
Where would you like to place the steps?

1362
00:56:40,338 --> 00:56:41,808
Would you like them here?

1363
00:56:41,968 --> 00:56:43,537
- After opening up the right side, - Right.

1364
00:56:43,538 --> 00:56:45,307
- this side seems better. - This way?

1365
00:56:45,308 --> 00:56:46,478
- Right. - This way? Got it.

1366
00:56:46,748 --> 00:56:47,778
Thank you.

1367
00:56:48,008 --> 00:56:49,117
I still haven't decided.

1368
00:56:49,118 --> 00:56:50,838
- Will you be using this as the mat? - Yes.

1369
00:56:51,048 --> 00:56:53,448
You should use a thin mat for a bunk bed.

1370
00:56:53,688 --> 00:56:54,748
Why is that?

1371
00:56:55,218 --> 00:56:57,757
- You need space for the ceiling. - Right. The ceiling.

1372
00:56:57,758 --> 00:56:58,758
- Right. - I see.

1373
00:56:59,428 --> 00:57:01,257
I should use this top bunk just for sleeping then.

1374
00:57:01,258 --> 00:57:02,297
You can do that.

1375
00:57:02,298 --> 00:57:03,298
(Chuckling)

1376
00:57:03,299 --> 00:57:04,497
It's exciting...

1377
00:57:04,498 --> 00:57:06,127
- to make your own space. - Right.

1378
00:57:06,128 --> 00:57:07,967
- I'm curious how it will look. - In her imagination,

1379
00:57:07,968 --> 00:57:10,268
- the perfect setup is already made. - Right.

1380
00:57:11,468 --> 00:57:14,507
(Gyeong Hye bought some coffee.)

1381
00:57:14,508 --> 00:57:16,338
- Have a sip of this first. - Right.

1382
00:57:18,708 --> 00:57:20,008
(Taking out)

1383
00:57:20,978 --> 00:57:23,148
- Wipe your sweat with this. - Right. Thank you.

1384
00:57:23,518 --> 00:57:25,747
- It got so hot, right? - Right.

1385
00:57:25,748 --> 00:57:27,387
- She's a bright person. - She's really bright.

1386
00:57:27,388 --> 00:57:28,618
- Right. - Right.

1387
00:57:29,688 --> 00:57:30,987
You know how it's even more confusing...

1388
00:57:30,988 --> 00:57:32,658
when you're familiar with it, right?

1389
00:57:32,988 --> 00:57:35,228
It must be tougher for you when the weather gets hotter.

1390
00:57:35,828 --> 00:57:37,758
- The weather... - It's still quite heavy.

1391
00:57:38,358 --> 00:57:40,498
It's bigger than what I expected.

1392
00:57:41,368 --> 00:57:44,968
It's always like this. It's my first time living alone.

1393
00:57:45,638 --> 00:57:47,567
You're setting up my first bunk bed...

1394
00:57:47,568 --> 00:57:48,768
at my first house.

1395
00:57:49,308 --> 00:57:50,507
- But... - It's an honor.

1396
00:57:50,508 --> 00:57:51,808
No. I should be honored. But...

1397
00:57:53,408 --> 00:57:56,278
Gosh, it's a lot more than what I expected.

1398
00:57:56,578 --> 00:57:57,877
Did you do that on purpose?

1399
00:57:57,878 --> 00:58:01,318
(You're doing fine, right?)

1400
00:58:02,618 --> 00:58:04,957
From afar, one might think she's a ghost living in this house.

1401
00:58:04,958 --> 00:58:06,427
(The ghost of small talk up close)

1402
00:58:06,428 --> 00:58:08,264
- An earth-bound spirit. - A ghost stuck in this house.

1403
00:58:08,288 --> 00:58:12,028
I was an installer of air conditioners in the past.

1404
00:58:12,568 --> 00:58:14,467
Those clients are the most burdensome.

1405
00:58:14,468 --> 00:58:15,598
- Gosh! - Really?

1406
00:58:15,898 --> 00:58:18,338
- Why is that? - I'm serious.

1407
00:58:18,398 --> 00:58:20,337
- Let me explain. - She praised him...

1408
00:58:20,338 --> 00:58:21,637
- and got him coffee. - Well,

1409
00:58:21,638 --> 00:58:22,937
giving him coffee was great.

1410
00:58:22,938 --> 00:58:24,637
- Giving him coffee was great, - Right.

1411
00:58:24,638 --> 00:58:26,277
But he might get nervous that way.

1412
00:58:26,278 --> 00:58:27,454
Because she's looking at him all the time.

1413
00:58:27,478 --> 00:58:29,217
(Staring)

1414
00:58:29,218 --> 00:58:30,617
That might make him feel nervous.

1415
00:58:30,618 --> 00:58:32,717
I'm bad at having small talks,

1416
00:58:32,718 --> 00:58:34,647
so I love it when people talk to me like that.

1417
00:58:34,648 --> 00:58:35,718
- Really? - Thank you.

1418
00:58:35,918 --> 00:58:37,257
- Gyeong Hye is just like me. - Right.

1419
00:58:37,258 --> 00:58:40,457
I keep having small talks with everyone.

1420
00:58:40,458 --> 00:58:42,127
Whenever we have team dinners together,

1421
00:58:42,128 --> 00:58:44,227
we're the only ones left after our small talks.

1422
00:58:44,228 --> 00:58:46,427
We talk about all sorts of things together.

1423
00:58:46,428 --> 00:58:48,597
- We talk endlessly. - The others get sick of it.

1424
00:58:48,598 --> 00:58:50,038
(The others get sick of it.)

1425
00:58:50,838 --> 00:58:52,097
Why would they get sick of it?

1426
00:58:52,098 --> 00:58:53,708
(We love small talks.)

1427
00:58:54,038 --> 00:58:55,167
- Bring it up. - Right.

1428
00:58:55,168 --> 00:58:56,277
It isn't heavy.

1429
00:58:56,278 --> 00:58:58,678
(The mattress is placed to finish things off.)

1430
00:59:00,408 --> 00:59:01,408
(Screaming)

1431
00:59:02,348 --> 00:59:05,247
(Screaming)

1432
00:59:05,248 --> 00:59:07,547
- Oh, my gosh. She's draining me. - She's so cute.

1433
00:59:07,548 --> 00:59:08,648
"My dream!"

1434
00:59:10,418 --> 00:59:11,687
(Gyeong Hye's dream finally becomes true.)

1435
00:59:11,688 --> 00:59:13,157
- It's nice. - There's more space now.

1436
00:59:13,158 --> 00:59:14,388
- It looks cozy. - Right.

1437
00:59:19,568 --> 00:59:21,027
(It's nice!)

1438
00:59:21,028 --> 00:59:22,068
Good!

1439
00:59:22,798 --> 00:59:24,768
(Delighted)

1440
00:59:25,338 --> 00:59:27,307
It was something I dreamed of since I was a kid.

1441
00:59:27,308 --> 00:59:28,338
I feel like...

1442
00:59:28,738 --> 00:59:30,677
- I'm about to shed tears. - Right.

1443
00:59:30,678 --> 00:59:31,738
(Tearing up)

1444
00:59:31,838 --> 00:59:33,677
- It was a touching moment. - She looks emotional.

1445
00:59:33,678 --> 00:59:35,724
- That would make her tear up. - I dreamed of it for a while.

1446
00:59:35,748 --> 00:59:38,077
The thing that I dreamed of...

1447
00:59:38,078 --> 00:59:40,588
is placed right before my eyes.

1448
00:59:41,118 --> 00:59:42,118
Gosh.

1449
00:59:43,018 --> 00:59:44,617
I can't really grasp what kind of emotion it was,

1450
00:59:44,618 --> 00:59:46,258
but I felt really happy.

1451
00:59:47,588 --> 00:59:50,898
I hesitate to start things as I'm always full of fear.

1452
00:59:51,358 --> 00:59:53,327
I'm starting to feel emotional after watching the clip.

1453
00:59:53,328 --> 00:59:55,297
I always think so much before making a decision.

1454
00:59:55,298 --> 00:59:57,968
That was why it took me so long to decide to live alone.

1455
00:59:58,198 --> 01:00:02,478
The fact that I did something out of confidence...

1456
01:00:03,008 --> 01:00:04,278
You're so kind.

1457
01:00:04,708 --> 01:00:06,548
You're so kind.

1458
01:00:08,078 --> 01:00:09,318
It didn't even touch her eyes.

1459
01:00:09,778 --> 01:00:10,778
(She did this.)

1460
01:00:10,779 --> 01:00:12,717
- Well... - I've never seen that before.

1461
01:00:12,718 --> 01:00:14,247
- Right. - What was that?

1462
01:00:14,248 --> 01:00:16,417
Well, I didn't want my makeup to get on his handkerchief.

1463
01:00:16,418 --> 01:00:17,487
- I'm wearing makeup today. - She's so considerate.

1464
01:00:17,488 --> 01:00:18,857
She's considerate with everything she does.

1465
01:00:18,858 --> 01:00:20,827
Thank you so much, Sung Hwan.

1466
01:00:20,828 --> 01:00:22,427
(A heartwarming battle of being kind)

1467
01:00:22,428 --> 01:00:24,557
When you move out, give the company a call...

1468
01:00:24,558 --> 01:00:26,997
and someone will come to help you uninstall the bed.

1469
01:00:26,998 --> 01:00:28,758
I wish it would be you when that time comes.

1470
01:00:29,028 --> 01:00:30,397
- Is that so? - Right.

1471
01:00:30,398 --> 01:00:32,098
- That would be great. - She's so cute.

1472
01:00:32,298 --> 01:00:33,968
- He won't answer the call. - Goodbye.

1473
01:00:34,868 --> 01:00:36,607
I would've collapsed after getting home if I were him.

1474
01:00:36,608 --> 01:00:38,354
- I must've been too excited. - He must feel drained.

1475
01:00:38,378 --> 01:00:40,178
- Gosh, it looks great. - Feeling drained?

1476
01:00:40,848 --> 01:00:42,548
(She feels great.)

1477
01:00:43,078 --> 01:00:45,717
(She dusts off her blanket with this great feeling.)

1478
01:00:45,718 --> 01:00:47,518
(Is she dancing?)

1479
01:00:48,548 --> 01:00:51,118
(Gyeong Hye gets done with her touching house renewal.)

1480
01:00:52,058 --> 01:00:53,158
Okay.

1481
01:00:54,558 --> 01:00:55,788
Here are the sheets.

1482
01:00:56,398 --> 01:00:57,527
Sheets? For the sink?

1483
01:00:57,528 --> 01:00:58,927
- I'll give it a try. - The green part?

1484
01:00:58,928 --> 01:01:00,627
- It's to make it look neat. - Right.

1485
01:01:00,628 --> 01:01:02,567
Just that part is green.

1486
01:01:02,568 --> 01:01:04,697
- Right. - That part does look off.

1487
01:01:04,698 --> 01:01:07,807
I bought them to make it match with the color on top.

1488
01:01:07,808 --> 01:01:09,528
I think it will look a lot better that way.

1489
01:01:10,108 --> 01:01:11,108
All right.

1490
01:01:11,109 --> 01:01:13,807
(Let's check the instructions first.)

1491
01:01:13,808 --> 01:01:14,848
Instructions.

1492
01:01:17,918 --> 01:01:20,388
Place it so that all sides can be covered.

1493
01:01:21,488 --> 01:01:25,288
(She positions herself in front of the target.)

1494
01:01:25,618 --> 01:01:26,827
All sides? Gosh!

1495
01:01:26,828 --> 01:01:28,187
(Gyeong Hye places the sheet.)

1496
01:01:28,188 --> 01:01:29,898
(Gosh!)

1497
01:01:30,198 --> 01:01:32,157
- Was this custom-made or what? - It fits perfectly.

1498
01:01:32,158 --> 01:01:33,167
- Right? - Right.

1499
01:01:33,168 --> 01:01:34,227
It's the perfect size.

1500
01:01:34,228 --> 01:01:35,788
Don't things feel great from the start?

1501
01:01:36,498 --> 01:01:37,897
This is fascinating. It fits perfectly.

1502
01:01:37,898 --> 01:01:40,108
All right. I got it.

1503
01:01:40,738 --> 01:01:42,508
Just remove around 10cm.

1504
01:01:43,978 --> 01:01:45,108
Gosh, my hands are shaking.

1505
01:01:47,048 --> 01:01:48,208
It must be done at once.

1506
01:01:49,478 --> 01:01:51,978
It rolls up so much. Hold on.

1507
01:01:54,088 --> 01:01:55,217
(She places the sheet gently on the side of the sink.)

1508
01:01:55,218 --> 01:01:56,717
- Please! - There must be no bubbles.

1509
01:01:56,718 --> 01:01:57,787
The top part must be applied well.

1510
01:01:57,788 --> 01:01:59,557
- I'm terrible with those things. - It must be a good start.

1511
01:01:59,558 --> 01:02:00,958
- No air should go in! - No!

1512
01:02:01,858 --> 01:02:04,258
(She keeps going while pressing it with her hand.)

1513
01:02:04,858 --> 01:02:08,628
(She's completely focusing while keeping her breath in.)

1514
01:02:09,468 --> 01:02:10,698
(Gosh!)

1515
01:02:11,168 --> 01:02:12,198
Please.

1516
01:02:14,068 --> 01:02:15,108
Oh, yes!

1517
01:02:15,638 --> 01:02:17,308
(She manages to get it stuck.)

1518
01:02:17,708 --> 01:02:18,877
(She rubs against it to get rid of the air.)

1519
01:02:18,878 --> 01:02:19,878
There you go.

1520
01:02:20,908 --> 01:02:22,617
(Hold on!)

1521
01:02:22,618 --> 01:02:23,677
Just like the screen protector.

1522
01:02:23,678 --> 01:02:26,418
(There's a bubble on one side.)

1523
01:02:27,448 --> 01:02:30,017
(There can't be any bubbles.)

1524
01:02:30,018 --> 01:02:31,958
- That's hard to do. - Right.

1525
01:02:33,958 --> 01:02:37,298
(She uses the scraper to remove the bubbles.)

1526
01:02:38,358 --> 01:02:40,528
I tried to apply the wallpaper on my own at home.

1527
01:02:41,628 --> 01:02:43,567
- There are bubbles everywhere. - You get bubbles.

1528
01:02:43,568 --> 01:02:45,397
- There are experts for a reason. - Right.

1529
01:02:45,398 --> 01:02:47,267
Right. But to call an expert,

1530
01:02:47,268 --> 01:02:48,967
- it was too expensive. - Right.

1531
01:02:48,968 --> 01:02:50,608
That's true as well.

1532
01:02:51,478 --> 01:02:53,918
(That was why the rookie tenant decided to do it on her own.)

1533
01:02:55,448 --> 01:02:57,118
- Gosh! - Gosh!

1534
01:02:57,448 --> 01:02:59,247
(What are we to do?)

1535
01:02:59,248 --> 01:03:00,288
There are bubbles.

1536
01:03:01,188 --> 01:03:03,157
- I should've pulled this side. - It's a huge bubble!

1537
01:03:03,158 --> 01:03:04,557
It should be removed.

1538
01:03:04,558 --> 01:03:06,657
It has to be removed to get it sorted.

1539
01:03:06,658 --> 01:03:08,158
(This wasn't what I wanted.)

1540
01:03:08,528 --> 01:03:09,897
(She urgently tries to fix it by pressing it with her hands.)

1541
01:03:09,898 --> 01:03:11,697
- Oh, no! - Oh, gosh!

1542
01:03:11,698 --> 01:03:13,127
(It's a mess.)

1543
01:03:13,128 --> 01:03:15,067
I hate seeing these things, Gyeong Hye.

1544
01:03:15,068 --> 01:03:16,708
(I hate seeing these things, Gyeong Hye.)

1545
01:03:17,368 --> 01:03:18,998
Gosh, Gyeong Hye!

1546
01:03:20,038 --> 01:03:22,368
I have to finish it off since I've started.

1547
01:03:23,238 --> 01:03:26,678
Let's be bold. Nice and bold.

1548
01:03:27,208 --> 01:03:29,977
(The result is a disaster.)

1549
01:03:29,978 --> 01:03:32,518
- I'm sorry. Gosh. - Oh, yes!

1550
01:03:32,918 --> 01:03:34,018
It's contemporary art.

1551
01:03:34,388 --> 01:03:36,187
(She keeps touching her work of art.)

1552
01:03:36,188 --> 01:03:38,588
- Gosh, it looks awful. - Gosh!

1553
