01:22:28,418 --> 01:22:30,687
I couldn't have a proper meal.

2059
01:22:30,688 --> 01:22:32,464
You need to eat before you sleep since you'd be hungry.

2060
01:22:32,488 --> 01:22:34,728
- You can't fall asleep too. - Have something delicious.

2061
01:22:35,158 --> 01:22:36,758
(Opening)

2062
01:22:38,598 --> 01:22:39,928
(Smiling)

2063
01:22:40,158 --> 01:22:42,468
(Becoming lively again after seeing food)

2064
01:22:43,498 --> 01:22:44,967
That's right. The side dishes Chan Hyeong gave.

2065
01:22:44,968 --> 01:22:46,198
Gosh, it's full.

2066
01:22:47,098 --> 01:22:48,507
- I'm so excited. - I was so happy...

2067
01:22:48,508 --> 01:22:49,667
to have the side dishes from his mom.

2068
01:22:49,668 --> 01:22:51,178
- You look really happy. - Gosh!

2069
01:22:55,508 --> 01:22:58,147
You're putting them in a separate dish.

2070
01:22:58,148 --> 01:23:00,987
I didn't want them to go bad when she made them for me.

2071
01:23:00,988 --> 01:23:02,664
I wanted to keep them well and have them for a long time.

2072
01:23:02,688 --> 01:23:04,087
Gyeong Hye is really neat.

2073
01:23:04,088 --> 01:23:05,657
It's troublesome to put the side dishes in a separate dish...

2074
01:23:05,658 --> 01:23:06,818
after working.

2075
01:23:08,558 --> 01:23:10,498
(Turning on the lights for the mood)

2076
01:23:10,928 --> 01:23:12,297
Thank you for the food.

2077
01:23:12,298 --> 01:23:14,298
(A meal filled with the homemade dishes is ready.)

2078
01:23:18,598 --> 01:23:19,897
(Taking a bite of the cockle first)

2079
01:23:19,898 --> 01:23:20,937
This is crazy.

2080
01:23:20,938 --> 01:23:22,168
- Gosh. - Seriously... Gosh.

2081
01:23:22,408 --> 01:23:23,408
(Exclaiming)

2082
01:23:24,978 --> 01:23:25,978
Gosh.

2083
01:23:28,408 --> 01:23:29,807
It's something you can't eat often...

2084
01:23:29,808 --> 01:23:31,978
- because it takes a lot of work. - That's right.

2085
01:23:35,118 --> 01:23:36,548
(Crunchy)

2086
01:23:37,518 --> 01:23:38,957
I feel like I'm eating it after work.

2087
01:23:38,958 --> 01:23:40,318
It was so good.

2088
01:23:40,858 --> 01:23:42,857
When you get home after work,

2089
01:23:42,858 --> 01:23:44,857
out of a need to compensate for your hard work...

2090
01:23:44,858 --> 01:23:45,957
You tend to eat more.

2091
01:23:45,958 --> 01:23:47,558
I'd turn on the delivery app right away.

2092
01:23:48,328 --> 01:23:51,598
(It's even more delicious because she worked hard.)

2093
01:23:52,538 --> 01:23:53,838
As for living alone,

2094
01:23:54,038 --> 01:23:56,968
it has clear pros and cons.

2095
01:23:57,068 --> 01:23:58,237
One of the pros is that...

2096
01:23:58,238 --> 01:24:00,377
you can focus on yourself solely...

2097
01:24:00,378 --> 01:24:02,448
because you're by yourself in that space.

2098
01:24:02,778 --> 01:24:04,077
"What should I eat today?"

2099
01:24:04,078 --> 01:24:05,448
"I find that uncomfortable."

2100
01:24:05,548 --> 01:24:06,817
It keeps coming back to me.

2101
01:24:06,818 --> 01:24:08,547
But when you live with family,

2102
01:24:08,548 --> 01:24:10,658
it becomes, "What should we have for dinner today?"

2103
01:24:11,188 --> 01:24:14,128
The con is that when it comes to something you haven't tried,

2104
01:24:14,288 --> 01:24:16,658
you could get flustered a lot or feel discouraged.

2105
01:24:16,888 --> 01:24:19,328
But if the pro can beat the con...

2106
01:24:19,428 --> 01:24:21,768
even by one percent,

2107
01:24:21,998 --> 01:24:23,827
it's worth a try.

2108
01:24:23,828 --> 01:24:27,438
It's a time when you get to learn about yourself.

2109
01:24:31,808 --> 01:24:35,647
(I'm Learning About Myself)

2110
01:24:35,648 --> 01:24:36,977
